    "body": "Source: ENGLISH SE PART 2.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nComprehensive & Ultimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nEduPro PH Reviewer\nSECONDARY EDUCATION - ENGLISH PART 2 2025/2026\nd. MACBETH\n1. Raul S. Manglapus once said:\nI have done this against the advice of a friend. He\n8. WHO SAID, “Ask not what tour country can\nfelt that since I would speak of Filipino movies.. I\ndo for you, but what you can do for you country?”\nshould instead begin by making you cry.\na. Richard M. Nixon\nWhich Filipino character is demonstrated in his\nb. John F. Kennedy\nspeech?\nc. Dwight D. Eisenhower\na. “Kanya-Kanya” syndrome\nd. Lyndon B. Johnson’\nb. “Hiya “\nc. “Palakasan at pataasan”culture\n9. Identify the poem from which the stanza is\nd. “Utang-na-loob”\ntake: Trust no future, howe’er pleasant\nLet the dead Past bury its dead!\n2. Which BEST described the READING AND\nAct-act in the living Present Heart within, and God\nTHE WRITING PROCESSES?\no’erhead\na. The stages occur in sequence\na. HYMN TO THE NIGHT\nb. The arrangement implies that the different\nb. THE CROSS OF SHOW\nlanguage arts develop separately\nc. MY LOST YOUTH\nc. The different stages merge and repeat\nd. A PSALM OF LIFE\nd. Children different mental process for\nreading, listening, talking and writing\n13. What does William Norris want you to do in\nhis ZIP THE LIP?\n3. Identify the poem from the lines are taken:\nIf your lips would keep from slips. Five things\nHave glimpse that would make me less forlorn;\nobserve with care;\nHave sight of Proteus rising from the sea;\nTo whom you speak; of whom you speak And how,\nOr hear old Triton blow is wreathed horn\nwhen, and where\na. Auguries of Innocence\na. To be truthful\nb. God Moves in a Mysterious Way\nb. To be sincere\nc. Elegy Written in a Country Churchyard\nc. To show kindness\nd. The World is Too Much With Us\nd. To observe confidentiality\n4. Identify the author of the poem torn which\nthe following lines are taken:\nO is she rosely loved\nis she lovely rosed\nO is she lovely sung as sea-shells?\na. Fernando M. Maramag\nb. Mauro Mendez\nc. Natividad Marquaez\nd. Jose Garcia Villa\n\n14. Identify the poem from which the lines are\ntaken: Oh’ Lift me as a wave a lead, a cloud!\nI fall upon the thorns of life! I bleed!\nA heavy weight of hours has chan’d and bow’d One\ntoo like thee-tameless, and swift, and proud.\na. Ode to the West Wind\nb. Crossing the Bar\nc. Ode to Evening\nd. My Last Duckess\n\n5. Who said, “These are the times that try\nmen’s souls?”\na. James Madison\nb. Thomas Paine\nc. Benjamin Franklin\nd. Thomas Jefferson\n\n15. What figure of speech is used in the lines\nbelow?\nHis bright eyes rolled, they never seemed to settle.\nAnd glittered like the flowers beneath a kettle:\nGeoffrey Chancer, The Canterbury Tales\na. Simile\nb. Hyperbole\nc. Metaphor\nd. Personification\n\n6. Who wrote the novel WAR AND PEACE?\na. Spencer\nb. Turgenew\nc. Shaw\nd. Tolstoy\n7. Identify the play from which the lines are\ntake: All that glitters is not gold;\nOften you have heard that told;\nMany a man his life hath sold But my outside to\nbehold; Glided tombs do norms enfold.\na. MECHANT OF VENICE\nb. HAMLET\nc. AS YOU LIKE IT\n\n16. Which TYPE reading is CHORAL READING?\na. Buddy\nb. Shared\nc. Guided\nd. Reading aloud to students\n17. Of the different principles of effectives\nteaching of reading, which is IMPROPERLY stated?\na. Effective teachers use the four cueing\nsystem to support students\nb. Effective teachers used instructional\n\nComprehensive & Ultimate LET Reviewer (2025-2026)\nEduPro PH Reviewer\napproaches on how children learn\nc. Effective teachers go out of the structured\nclassrooms to create community of readers\nd. Effective teachers select appropriate\nreading materials\n18. Which languages system is focused on\nVOCABULARY?\na. Syntactic\nb. Pragmatic\nc. Semantics\nd. Phonological\n19. Which theory claims that readers have\ndifficulty in comprehension because they are\nfocused on WORD IDENTIFICATION?\na. Submersion\nb. Automaticity\nc. Alphabetic\nd. Immersion\n20. Which speech is considered of the greatest\nspeeches for its vision of American democracy by a\nU.S political leader?\na. THE GETTYS BURG ADDRESS\nb. John F Kennedy’s INAUGURAL SPEECH\nc. LINCOLNMEMORIAL ADDRESS\nd. Patrick Henry’s speech\n21. Which play of Jose M. Hernandez tells of an\nartisan who forged cannons for the use of the\nSpaniards?\na. THE REAL LEADER\nb. PANDAY PIRA\nc. THE FILIPINO REBEL\nd. THE CRY OF THE PHILIPPINES\n22. If Dick’s father is John’s son, what relation\nhas Dick to John?\na. Nephew\nb. Brother\nc. Son\nd. Grandson\n23. Consider these lines from “The Ideal wife”:\nFAVOR IS DECEITFULL AND BEAUTY IS VAIN BUT\nWOMAN THAT FEARETH THE LORD, SHE SHALL\nBE PRAISED\nWhich word infers the moral of the verse?\na. Praised\nb. Feareth\nc. Favor\nd. Beauty\n24. Which novel written by Kerima-Tuvera tells\nof the story of Emma Mercene who struggles for\nconsummation of purse and clean love?\na. THE BARAGAY\nb. THE HAND OF THE ENEMY\nc. A CHILD OF SORROW\nd. THE FILIPINO REBEL\n25. William Wordsworth wrote “SHE WAS\nPHANTOM OF DELIGHT” from which the lines are",
