    "body": "Source: 4. LORIMAR - ENGLISH SPECIALIZATION (BOOK 2).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nLicense_Sure ENGLISH MAJOR LET REVIEWER\nVOLUME 2\na. Diagnostic Test\nb. Placement Test\nc. Proficiency Test\nd. Achievement Test\n251. Which type of test is administered at the beginning or middle of the term and are aimed at\nfostering achievement by promoting strengths and eliminating the weaknesses of individual\nstudents?\na. Diagnostic Test\nb. Placement Test\nc. Proficiency Test\nd. Achievement Test\n252. Which of the following is NOT an objective of a diagnostic test?\na. Determine what existing knowledge, skills, attitudes, interests and needs the students had\nb. Determine the range of individual differences\nc. Determine what program or modifications are required to meet the needs of individuals\nd. Determine the level of study that the student would benefit from\n253. The following questions all pertain to validity EXCEPT ______.\na. do all the items to be measuring the same thing?\nb. does the test cover all aspects of what it claims to measure?\nc. do the test items look like realistic, authentic uses of what is being measured?\nd. does the test meet the limits of existing resources including time and test administration?\n254. Who among the following teachers is doing formative assessment?\na. Ms. Canlas who asked series of questions I nthe middle of the lecture to determine if students\nunderstood the concepts\nb. Mr. Galang who gave a test at the end of the grading period to determine if the goals of the\nprogram are met\nc. Ms. Tulabut who gave a test to determine what students know before the unit begins\nd. Ms. Jaochico who gave a test at the end of the semester to determine if the course outsomes\nare met\n255. The effect of testing on teaching and learning is known as ________.\na. wash back\nb. construct\nc. auditability\nd. credibility\n256. Ms. Cruz wants to measure the language abilities of her students using the direct testing.\nWhich of the following is NOT recommended?\na. Writing letters\nb. Role-play\nc. Cloze test\nd. Information gap task\n257. The following are examples of discrete point testing EXCEPT ______.\na. essay writing\nb. spelling test\nc. yes/no question\n\nLICENSURE EXAMINATION for TEACHERS\n\nPage 40\n\nLicense_Sure ENGLISH MAJOR LET REVIEWER\nVOLUME 2\nd. true-false answer\n258. Dr. Tubera uses alternative methods of assessment. Which will he NOT likely use?\na. Multiple Choice Test\nb. Reflective Journal Writing\nc. Oral Presentation\nd. Developing Portfolios\n259. Mrs. David is going to construct a test in English. What must she do first?\na. Write the test items\nb. List down the test objectives\nc. Let an expert validate the test\nd. Prepare a table of specifications\n260. Which of the following is an example is an example of a beneficial backwash?\na. If the skill of writing is tested only by multiple choice items, there is a great pressure to\npractice such items.\nb. If teachers ignore the subjects and activities which do not contribute directly to passing the\nexam.\nc. If a test is regarded as important, preparation for it can dominate teaching activities.\nd. If what is assessed becomes what is valued and what is valued becomes what is taught.\n261. A test pretended to measure pronunciation ability but did not require the test taker to speak\nmight be thought to lack of _______.\na. concurrent validity\nb. content validity\nc. test-rater reliability\nd. test-administration reliability\n15. LANGUAGE RESEARCH\n15.3 Apply principles and approaches to find answers to questions in language\nand literature teaching and learning\n262. Which of the following explains why research is empirical?\na. Research to based on data perceived by the senses.\nb. Research follows procedures.\nc. Research must be based on facts.\nd. Research makes use of tools.\n263. Which of the following explains why research is systematic?\na. Research to based on data perceived by the senses.\nb. Research follows procedures.\nc. Research must be based on facts.\nd. Research makes use of tools.\n264. Which is NOT a research tool?\na. Questionnaires\nb. Checklist\nc. Test\nd. Grades\n\nLICENSURE EXAMINATION for TEACHERS\n\nPage 41\n\nLicense_Sure ENGLISH MAJOR LET REVIEWER\nVOLUME 2\n265. If researchers test the feasibility of using cell phone as vocabulary gadget, what purpose of\nresearch are they NOT likely to achieve?\na. Discover a substance.\nb. Improve a product.\nc. Validate generalizations.\nd. Verify existing knowledge.\n266. If researchers want to know if most English majors have English as their favorite subject,\nwhat purpose of research are they likely to achieve?\nb. Improve a product.\nc. Validate generalizations.\nd. Verify existing knowledge.\n267. Which research problem is clearly directive in nature?\na. What Topic to Have in the Next Seminars\nb. How to Improve Services in the Canteen\nc. Why Students Wear Glasses\nd. Which Sectioning Scheme to Follow\n268. Which research has classroom as its locale?\na. Experimental\nb. Descriptive\nc. Action\nd. Analytical\n269. If the research is quantitative, which finding should it focus on?\na. Fifty six of students do not pass assignments requiring reading.\nb. Two out of 69 participants abide by the English Only Policy.\nc. Teachers slowly tap the shoulders of their students while consoling them.\nd. An interview said that he usually has nightmares when he sleeps right after eating.\n270. If researcher want to know why teacher do not erase writings on the board to make them\neventually erase, what type of research are they into?\na. Propriety\nb. Pure\nc. Behavioral\nd. Communication\n271. Which type of research is likely to lead to the discovery of a new theory?\na. Experimental\nb. Phenomenological\nc. Holistic\nd. Scholarly\n272. What is the aim of a research proposal?\na. To present an entire research\nb. To defend findings\nc. To suggest a planned study\nd. To find solution to a research problem\n\nLICENSURE EXAMINATION for TEACHERS\n\nPage 42",
