    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n75. Tom gave us ________ apples.\nA) a lot of\nB) so much\nC) same\n\nBook 1 Part E\n\nD) sang\n\nD) come\n\n96. What ________ behind the house when you were a child?\nA) was there\nB) there were C) were there\nD) there was\n\nD) every\n\n71. When ________, I’ll talk to him.\nA) does Peter come\nB) Peter will come\nC) Peter comes\nD) can Peter come\n\n74. Is Chris ________ Kate?\nA) taller that\nB) so tall as\n\nB) That’s him.\nD) Mr Smith is the old man.\n\n94. Last week John ________ his leg.\nA) felt and broken\nB) fell and broke\nC) feels and breaks\nD) fallen and broken\n\nD) any people\n\nB) is the same as me\nD) is the same I am\n\n70. Cathie has read ________ French books.\nA) so much\nB) a few\nC) the more\n\nD) a mine\n\n97. What date is it? It’s ________ .\nA) the July fourth.\nC) of July the fourth.\n\nB) the fourth of July.\nD) fourth July.\n\n98. My car was ________ .\nA) in front of the his\nC) in front the his\n\nB) in front of his\nD) in front of he’s\n\n99. Jack ________ his thick coat because it was snowing.\nA) puts on\nB) put on\nC) takes on\nD) took on\n\nD) taller as\n\n100. A) Was the big brown book?\nC) Was the big book brown?\n\nB) Was the brown book a big?\nD) Was the brown a big book?\n\nD) this\n\n202\n\nElementary test 6\n\nINTERMEDIATE TEST - 1\n25. ________ at the moment, I’ll go to the shops.\nA) For it doesn’t rain\nB) As it doesn’t rain\nC) For it isn’t raining\nD) As it isn’t raining\n\nChoose the correct answer. Only one answer is correct.\nLast June my brother __1__ a car. He had had an old scooter before,\nbut it __2__ several times during the spring. “What you want is a second\n- hand Mini,” I suggested. “If you give me the money,” he said, “__3__\none tomorrow.” “I can’t give you the money,” I replied, “but what about\nAunt Myra. She must have enough. We __4__ her since Christmas but\nshe always hints that we __5__ go and see her more often.”\nWe told our parents where we were going. They weren’t very happy\nabout it and asked us not to go. So __6__ But later that same day\nsomething strange __7__. A doctor __8__ us that Aunt Myra __9__ into\nhospital for an operation. “__10__ go and see her at the same time,” said\nmy mother. “You two go today, but don’t mention the money.”\nWhen we __11__ Aunt Myra __12__ “I’m not seriously ill,” she said,\n“but the doctor insist that __13__ to drive my car. You can have it if you\npromise __14__ me to the seaside now and again.” We agreed, and now\nwe quite enjoy our monthly trips to the coast with Aunt Myra.\n1.\n\nA) wanted to buy\nC) liked to buy\n\nB) wanted buying\nD) liked buying\n\n2.\n\nA) was breaking down\nC) had broken down\n\nB) was breaking up\nD) had broken up\n\n3.\n\nA) I get\nC) I’m going to get\n\nB) I’m going\nD) I’ll get\n\n4.\n\nA) are not seeing\nC) didn’t see\n\nB) haven’t seen\nD) don’t see\n\n5.\n\nA) should\n\nC) would\n\n6.\n\nA) that we haven’t\nC) we haven’t\n\nB) that we didn’t\nD) we didn’t\n\n7.\n\nA) occurred\nC) passed\n\nB) took the place\nD) was there\n\n8.\n\nA) rang for telling\nC) rung for telling\n\nB) rang to tell\nD) rung to tell\n\n9.\n\nA) had gone\n\nC) has gone\n\nB) shall\n\nB) had been\n\n26. Bill drinks ________ whisky.\nA) any\nB) none\n\nC) too many\n\nD) so much\n\n27. ________ are very intelligent.\nA) Both of them B) Both them\n\nC) Both they\n\nD) The both\n\n28. In a shop ________ customers.\nA) it is important pleasing\nB) it is important to please\nC) there is important pleasing D) there is important to please\n29. Don’t leave your shoes on the table.\nA) Put off them!\nB) Take them off!\nC) Pick them off!\nD) Pick up them!\n30. ________ in my class likes the teacher.\nA) All persons B) All pupils\nC) Everyone\n\nD) All people\n\n31. We expected about 20 girls but there were ________ people there.\nA) another\nB) others\nC) some\nD) more\n32. Your bicycle shouldn’t be in the house!\nA) Take it out! B) Get out it!\nC) Put it off!\n\nD) Take away it!\n\n33. What time does the bus ________ Bradford?\nA) go away to B) go away for C) leave to\n\nD) leave for\n\n34. She ________ be Canadian because she’s got a British passport.\nA) can’t\nB) isn’t able to C) mustn’t\nD) doesn’t need\n35. “Our daughter ________”, they said.\nA) was born since three years\nB) is born for three years ago\nC) was born three years ago\nD) has been born since three years ago\n\nD) will\n\n36. When ________ English?\nA) has he begun to study\nC) did he begin to study\n\nB) has he begun study\nD) did he begin study\n\n37. Do you want some cheese? No, ________ .\nA) I’ve some still\nB) I still haven’t much\nC) I don’t want\nD) I’ve still got much\n\nD) has been\n\n10. A) We may not all\nC) All we can’t\n\nB) We can’t all\nD) All we may not\n\n38. Brenda likes going to the theatre and ________ .\nA) so do I\nB) so go I\nC) so I like\nD) so I am\n\n11. A) have come there\nC) got there\n\nB) were arriving\nD) came to there\n\n39. ________ from London to Edinburgh!\nA) How long there is\nB) What a long way it is\nC) What distance is there\nD) How long is\n\n12. A) was seeming quite happily\nC) seemed quite happily\n\nB) was seeming quite happy\nD) seemed quite happy\n\n13. A) I’m getting so old\nC) I get so old\n\nB) I’m getting too old\nD) I get too old\n\n14. A) taking\n\nC) to take\n\nB) bringing\n\n15. Can this camera ________ good photos?\nA) make\nB) to make\nC) take\n\n40. He’s a good guitarist, but he plays the piano ________ .\nA) quite well\nB) too hardly\nC) very good\nD) much better\n41. When you go to the shops, bring me ________ .\nA) a fruit tin\nB) a fruits tin\nC) a tin of fruit D) a tin of fruits\n\nD) to bring\n\n42. Molly doesn’t eat fish.\nA) So doesn’t John.\nC) John doesn’t too.\n\nD) to take\n\nB) Neither does John.\nD) John doesn’t that either.\n\n16. Who was the first person ________ today?\nA) spoke to you\nB) you spoke to\nC) you spoke\nD) whom you spoke\n\n43. The airport i