every day someone goes to the hospital __13__. She’s a\nlot better now.” “I’m glad to hear that,” said Jack. “Anyway __14__ coffee.”\n\n26. I’ve just seen Mary ________ the village.\nA) to walk towards\nB) to walk against\nC) walking towards\nD) walking against\n27. Sally didn’t put in ________ water.\nA) no\nB) so much\nC) enough of\n28. ________ like ice-cream.\nA) Every children\nC) All of children\n\nD) few\n\nB) Every child\nD) All children\n\n29. When you go abroad, do you ________ take your passport?\nA) have to\nB) ought to\nC) need\nD) must\n30. You don’t need your hat.\nA) Put off it!\nB) Put it off!\n\nC) Take off it!\n\nD) Take it off!\n\n1.\n\nA) Are you coming\nC) Do you come\n\nB) Are you going\nD) Do you go\n\n31. How many elephants did you see? ________ .\nA) None\nB) No one\nC) Not many ones D) No many\n\n2.\n\nA) since then we moved\nC) that we moved us\n\nB) since we moved\nD) that we move\n\n32. We’re going to go ________ car.\nA) in France in John’s\nB) in France by John’s\nC) to France in John’s\nD) to France by John’s\n\n3.\n\nA) you’re doing\nC) do you do\n\nB) you do\nD) takes you\n\n4.\n\nA) went the Oxford Street along\nB) was going Oxford Street along\nC) was going along Oxford Street\nD) went along the Oxford Street\nA) must\n\n6.\n\nA) was beaten with\nC) was beaten by\n\nB) was hit with\nD) was hit by\n\n7.\n\nA) Was she having\nC) Has she put\n\nB) Did she have\nD) She was wearing\n\n8.\n\nA) they were any\nC) they were any ones\n\nB) there were any\nD) there were any ones\n\n9.\n\nA) wasn’t badly hurt\nC) wasn’t so much hurt\n\nB) wasn’t hurt bad\nD) wasn’t too much hurt\n\nB) ought\n\nC) ought to\n\n34. What time does the train ________ Bristol?\nA) arrive into B) come at\nC) go into\n\n5.\n\n10. A) need\n\nB) had to\n\n33. It’s dark without the lights. Let’s ________ .\nA) switch on them\nB) turn them on\nC) to turn on them\nD) to switch them on\n\nC) should\n\nD) had better\n\nD) get to\n\n35. How ________ here?\nA) long you stay