touch its moves\nC) touch it moving\nD) feel it moving\n93. Sally never goes to pubs.\nA) Tom doesn’t that either.\nC) Neither does Tom.\n\nD) are all\n\nB) Tom doesn’t too.\nD) Tom does neither.\n\n94. Agnes was the first girl ________ when you got here.\nA) you talked to whom\nB) you talked to\nC) whom you talked\nD) who talked you\n\nB) anybody to see me\nD) anybody see me\n\n70. Can I ________ this book back to you?\nA) to take\nB) to bring\nC) take\n\nD) Put it on!\n\n83. We haven’t got a record player. Let’s ________ .\nA) to borrow the Mary’s\nB) borrow Mary’s\nC) to lend one of Mary\nD) lend Mary’s one\n\n67. The last time ________ to the library was last week.\nA) I have gone B) I have been C) I was\nD) I went\n\n69. I don’t want ________ .\nA) that anybody saw me\nC) that anybody sees me\n\nD) Few\n\n81. In some countries children normally go ________ bikes.\nA) to school on\nB) to the school on\nC) to school by\nD) to the school by\n\n66. My piano is magnificent ________ since I was 18.\nA) I got it\nB) I’ve got it\nC) I have it\nD) I’ve had it\n\n68. My parents ________ in this evening.\nA) are both\nB) all are\nC) both are\n\nD) these all\n\nC) all these\n\n80. ________ people came than I expected.\nA) Other\nB) Fewer\nC) Another\n\nD) get\n\nB) It looks marvelously\nD) It seems marvelously\n\n77. I like ________ two records.\nA) these both B) both these\n\n79. If you’ve read my book, please ________ to me.\nA) give it again B) give again it C) give it back D) give back it\n\nD) that she\n\n62. A) It looks to be marvelous\nC) It seems marvelous\n\nD) any\n\n78. To drive a car safely it is ________ good brakes.\nA) essential with\nB) essential having\nC) essential to have\nD) essential have\n\nD) can you\n\n57. A) explained him I liked\nC) told him I liked\n\n76. Jane had ________ furniture for her room.\nA) enough\nB) many\nC) all\n\n95. Many parents allow their children ________ own decisions.\nA) making their B) making the C) to make their D) to make 