    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n74. I don’t know where ________ .\nA) the lavatory to be\nB) is the lavatory\nC) be the lavatory\nD) the lavatory is\n75. We watched carefully ________ the houses.\nA) during she walked against\nB) during she walked towards\nC) while she walked against\nD) while she walked towards\n\nBook 1 Part E\n\nD) one\n\n99. Teresa wasn’t the only one in the car ________\nA) It was some other.\nB) It was someone else.\nC) There was some other.\nD) There was someone else.\n100. I’d like to leave my car near here. Where’s the ________ please?\nA) nearest parking\nB) next parking\nC) nearest car park\nD) next car park\n\n206\n\nIntermediate test 2\n\nINTERMEDIATE TEST - 3\n25. I’ve been looking for you ________ .\nA) everywhere B) anywhere\nC) for all places D) in all places\n\nChoose the correct answer. Only one answer is correct.\nI __1__ to your letter, which __2__ before __3__ for Rome. __4__\nyesterday that the company __5__ me there next week for a business\nconference. If I __6__ about it earlier I would have told you. Anyway, I’ll\nring you as soon as I __7__ there.\nJohn Marshall came into my office while I __8__ the arrangements\nfor my flight to Rome. You __9__ him last year when you were in England.\nIf you __10__ him, you would remember him because he is over two\nmeters tall. He told me that he __11__ for the previous two months on\nthe plans for the new factory in Naples. He __12__ very hard because he\nlooked very tired. By the time I come to Rome he __13__ them so I’ll\nbring them with me.\n1.\n\nA) like to reply\nC) would like to reply\n\nB) would like replying\nD) am wanting to reply\n\n2.\n\nA) arrived two days ago\nC) arrived since two days\n\nB) has arrived two days ago\nD) has arrived since two days\n\n3.\n\nA) to go out\n\nC) leave\n\n4.\n\nA) I was said\nC) I was told\n\nB) It was said me\nD) It was told me\n\n5.\n\nA) shall have sent\nC) shall be sending\n\nB) is going to send\nD) shall send\n\nA) knew\nC) would have known\n\nB) had known\nD) would know\n\n7.\n\nA) get\n\nB) will get\n\nC) shall get\n\nD) will have got\n\n8.\n\nA) made\n\nB) did make\n\nC) had made\n\nD) was making\n\n9.\n\nA) can have met\nC) can meet\n\n6.\n\n10. A) meet\n\nB) to leave\n\nB) met\n\n26. ________ he was tired he went on working.\nA) Even\nB) Yet\nC) Although\n\nD) In spite\n\n27. Send him to the baker’s ________ the bread.\nA) to buy\nB) in order he buys\nC) for to buy\nD) for buying\n28. Wanda is ________ Jane.\nA) a lot pretty than\nC) much more pretty that\n\nB) a lot prettier that\nD) much prettier than\n\n29. He didn’t know ________ or go home.\nA) to wait\nB) if that he should wait\nC) if to wait\nD) whether to wait\n30. ________ me ________ .\nA) Tell / what is this\nC) Say / what is this\n\nD) leaving\n\nB) Tell / what this is\nD) Say / what this is\n\n31. If you ________ help you, you only have to ask me.\nA) want me to\nB) want that I\nC) want I should\nD) are wanting me to\n32. “I’m going to the theatre tonight.” “So ________ ”\nA) will I\nB) I will\nC) am I\nD) do I\n\nB) may have met\nD) may meet\nC) were meeting D) would meet\n\n33. How ________ is it from here to New York?\nA) long way\nB) long\nC) far\n\nD) much far\n\n34. I wish I ________ what to do.\nA) knew\nB) have known C) know\n\nD) would know\n\n35. He likes playing ________\nA) the football B) football\n\nD) at the football\n\nC) at football\n\n11. A) has worked\nC) had been worked\n\nB) has been worked\nD) had been working\n\n36. My brother, ________ lives in Iceland, is coming to visit us.\nA) which\nB) that\nC) whom\nD) who\n\n12. A) must have worked\nC) need have worked\n\nB) had to work\nD) needed to work\n\n37. He’s already about ________ his father.\nA) so tall than B) as tall than C) as tall as\n\nD) so tall as\n\n13. A) will finish\nC) will have finished\n\nB) will be finished\nD) has finished\n\n38. ________ him go out if he wants to.\nA) Allow\nB) Leave\nC) Let\n\nD) Permit\n\n39. I didn’t hear what he was ________\nA) telling\nB) saying\nC) talking\n\nD) speaking\n\n14. Take an umbrella ________ it rains.\nA) in any case B) in case\nC) because\n\nD) for\n\n15. I ________ have coffee than tea.\nA) like more to B) prefer\nC) would rather D) had better\n\n40. I ________ watching this program because it is very interesting.\nA) amuse\nB) please\nC) delight\nD) enjoy\n\n16. He didn’t thank me for the present. That is ________ annoyed me.\nA) the which\nB) that which\nC) the thing what\nD) what\n\n41. That student ________ his hand every time I ask a question.\nA) gets out\nB) gets up\nC) rises\nD) puts up\n\n17. I’ll have to buy ________ trousers.\nA) a\nB) two\nC) a pair of\n\n42. I ________ hands with him when he came in.\nA) gave\nB) greeted\nC) shook\n\n18. She looks ________ .\nA) pleasant\nC) that she’s pleasant\n\nD) a couple of\n\n43. He wants to get a better ________ and earn more money.\nA) job\nB) work\nC) employ\nD) employment\n\nB) to be pleasant\nD) pleasantly\n\n44. ________ the children for me while I’m out.\nA) Look after B) Look to\nC) Take care\n\n19. When you ________ the furniture, please tell me.\nA) will finish to move\nB) finish to move\nC) will finish moving\nD) have finished moving\n\n21. Don’t make him ________ it if he doesn’t want to.\nA) do\nB) to do\nC) doing\nD) that he do\n\n45. A) ball\n\nB) call\n\nC) fall\n\nD) shall\n\n46. A) freeze\n\nB) piece\n\nC) please\n\nD) trees\n\n47. A) lose\n\nB) chose\n\nC) rose\n\nD) nose\n\n48. A) what\n\nB) cat\n\nC) sat\n\nD) fat\n\n49. A) fair\n\nB) wear\n\nC) hear\n\nD) their\n\n50. A) days\n\nB) says\n\nC) ways\n\nD) plays\n\nD) probably\n\n23. She came ________ because her car has broken down.\nA) walking\nB) by foot\nC) with foot\nD) on foot\n24. That’s the man ________ yesterday.\nA) which I was talking to\nB) what I was talking to\nC) I was talking to\nD) with who I was talking\n\nBook 1 Part E\n\nD) Care\n\nIn this series of questions, three words have the same sound but\none does not. Choose the one that does not.\n\n20. The reason ________ I’m writing is to tell you about a party on\nSaturday.\nA) because\nB) why\nC) for\nD) as\n\n22. He’s ________ to know the answer.\nA) likely\nB) probable\nC) maybe\n\nD) offered\n\n207\n\nIntermediate test 3\n\n74. ________ he worked all day, he couldn’t finish the job.\nA) Although\nB) Even\nC) In case\nD) In spite",
