    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nB) will work\nD) will be working\n\n8.\n\nA) I’ve been said to\nC) It has been said to me\n\nB) I’ve been told to\nD) It has been told me\n\n9.\n\nA) would\nC) am wanting to\n\nB) would to\nD) want to\n\nB) to get\n\n10. A) the thief got in\nC) has the thief got in\n\nC) was falling\n\n27. ________ English?\nA) How long time are you studying\nB) How long do you study\nC) How long have you been studying\nD) How long time have you studied\n28. The little boy keeps the insect in a ________ .\nA) match box\nB) box of matches\nC) box of the matches\nD) box match\n\nD) have fallen\n\n29. She’s going to the photographer’s ________ .\nA) to take her photograph\nB) to have taken her photograph\nC) to have her photograph\nD) that he takes her photograph\n30. He looks ________ .\nA) to be unhappy\nC) unhappy\n\nD) to go\n\nB) unhappily\nD) that he’s unhappy\n\n31. Where have you been? I’ve been playing ________ .\nA) the tennis\nB) at tennis\nC) at the tennis D) tennis\n32. It’s very kind ________ invite me.\nA) from you to B) of you to\nC) by you to\n\nD) that you\n\n33. I can’t break. It’s ________ iron.\nA) as hard as B) so hard as\nC) as hard than D) so hard than\n34. I didn’t know ________ him or not.\nA) whether to help\nB) if to help\nC) to help\nD) if that I should help\n\nB) was the thief getting in\nD) did the thief get in\n\n11. A) had let\n\nB) had left\n\nC) was letting\n\nD) was leaving\n\n12. A) would be\n\nB) ought be\n\nC) should be\n\nD) had to be\n\n13. A) looked after\nC) have looked after\n\n26. He doesn’t know the answer ________ I’ve told him several times.\nA) in spite\nB) even\nC) while\nD) although\n\n35. ________ of them knew about the plan because it was secret.\nA) Some\nB) Any\nC) No one\nD) None\n36. Mont Blanc, ________ we visited last summer, is the highest\nmountain in Europe.\nA) where\nB) which\nC) that\nD) what\n\nB) looks after\nD) should look after\n\n37. This question is ________ difficult for me.\nA) so much\nB) too much\nC) too\n\n14. There are so many cars ________ nowadays.\nA) for all places\nB) in all the place\nC) anywhere\nD) everywhere\n\nD) enough\n\n38. It ________ the village where we spent our holidays last summer.\nA) reminds me of\nB) remembers me of\nC) reminds me to\nD) remembers me to\n\n15. Ask him to go to the post office ________ some stamps.\nA) to get\nB) for getting\nC) in order he gets\nD) that he gets\n16. The reason ________ I can’t come is that I have to work late.\nA) because\nB) for\nC) as\nD) why\n\n39. Living here at the top of the mountain with no one else near you\nmust be very ________ .\nA) sole\nB) alone\nC) only\nD) lonely\n\n17. She cut the cloth with ________ scissors.\nA) a couple of B) a pair of\nC) two\n\n40. The tailor made him a new ________ .\nA) clothes\nB) suit\nC) dress\n\n18. ________ me ________ .\nA) Tell / where are you going\nC) Say / where are you going\n\nD) a\n\n41. The clock ________ and we realized it was two o’clock.\nA) hit\nB) struck\nC) turned\nD) rang\n\nB) Tell / where you are going\nD) Say / where you are going\n\n19. The children ________ play with them.\nA) want that I\nB) want me for\nC) want me to\nD) are wanting that\n20. He may be able to come to the party. ________ the other hand, he\nmay be too busy.\nA) On\nB) In\nC) By\nD) For\n21. I haven’t seen him ________ .\nA) last week\nC) for last week\n\n23. John is ________ .\nA) a friend of me\nC) a friend of mine\n24. She’s the girl ________ .\nA) whose money was stolen\nC) whose money was robbed\n\nBook 1 Part E\n\n42. Good ________ ! I hope you win the race.\nA) sort\nB) wish\nC) luck\n\nD) chance\n\n43. My car ________ so I had to come by bus.\nA) fell down\nB) fell over\nC) broke down\n\nD) broke up\n\n44. Look what Father ________ me when he came home from work.\nA) brought\nB) took\nC) carried\nD) fetched\nIn this series of questions, three words have the same sound but\none does not. Choose the one that does not.\n\nB) during last week\nD) since last week\n\n22. I’m fond ________ good music.\nA) to the\nB) to\nC) of the\n\nD) wear\n\n45. A) force\n\nB) sauce\n\nC) horse\n\nD) worse\n\n46. A) good\n\nB) wood\n\nC) blood\n\nD) stood\n\n47. A) but\n\nB) put\n\nC) cut\n\nD) shut\n\n48. A) lost\n\nB) most\n\nC) post\n\nD) ghost\n\n49. A) talk\n\nB) pork\n\nC) fork\n\nD) work\n\n50. A) mass\n\nB) pass\n\nC) grass\n\nD) class\n\nD) of\n\nB) a friend mine\nD) one friend of mine\nB) the which money was stolen\nD) the which money was robbed\n\n209\n\nIntermediate test 4\n\n75. Who is responsible ________ the arrangements?\nA) for make\nB) to make\nC) to making\n\nI went to the doctor’s yesterday. I __51__ for half an hour before he\n__52__ see me. “I __53__ abroad next week,” I said. “I __54__ to Africa\non business. But __55__ two days. __56__ I’ll be well enough to go?”\n“When I __57__ you, I’ll be able to tell you,” the doctor said.\n“I __58__ in the garden when I suddenly felt the pain,” I told the\ndoctor. “If I __59__ immediately, it would have been all right, I suppose.\nBut I __60__ any exercise in my job so I went on working.” After __61__\nme carefully, the doctor said: “You __62__ a bone in your back. I __63__\nyou to hospital for an X-ray.”\n51. A) must wait\n\nB) had to wait\n\nC) should wait\n\nD) ought to wait\n\n52. A) can\n\nB) may\n\nC) might\n\nD) could\n\n53. A) shall be go\n\nB) will be go\n\nC) am going\n\nD) go\n\nD) for making\n\n76. Speak to him slowly ________ he will understand you better.\nA) in order\nB) so that\nC) for\nD) that\n77. He wanted to know ________ there.\nA) how long time I had been\nB) how long had I been\nC) how long time had I been\nD) how long I had been\n78. He works too hard. That is ________ is wrong with him.\nA) that which\nB) the what\nC) what\nD) the thing what\n79. I know it’s not important but I can’t help ________ about it.\nA) except to think\nB) thinking\nC) think\nD) to think\n\n54. A) am sent\nC) am send\n\nB) am being sent\nD) be sent\n\n55. A) I’ve had a pain for\nC) I’m having a pain for\n\nB) I’ve had a pain since\nD) I’m having a pain since\n\n56. A) Do you think\nC) Does you think\n\nB) Are you thinking\nD) You are thinking\n\n57. A) am examining\nC) will have examined\n\nB) will examine\nD) have examined\n\n58. A) worked\nC) was working\n\nB) have worked\nD) have been working\n\n59. A) had stopped\nC) stopped\n\nB) would have stopped\nD) would stop\n\n60. A) never get\nC) am never getting\n\nB) don’t get ever\nD) am not ever getting\n\n61. A) examine\nC) examining\n\nB) to examine\nD) that he had examined\n\n62. A) can be hurt\nC) can have hurt\n\nB) may be hurt\nD) may have hurt\n\n63. A) would send\nC) am wanting to send\n\nB) would like to send\nD) will like to send\n\n64. It’s ________ I expected.\nA) much bigger than\nC) a lot more big than\n\n87. That’s the man ________ killed my cat.\nA) whose dog\nB) the dog of whom\nC) which dog\nD) the which dog",
