    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nB) much bigger that\nD) a lot more big that\n\n88. I learnt how to ________ a bicycle when I was six years old.\nA) drive\nB) ride\nC) conduct\nD) lead\n\n80. He finally ________ the driving test after failing three times.\nA) succeeded in passing\nB) succeeded to pass\nC) could pass\nD) managed passing\n81. She’s very fond ________ modern art.\nA) of the\nB) of\nC) to the\n\n83. I won’t allow you ________ for the meal.\nA) pay\nB) paying\nC) to pay\nD) that you should pay\n84. She hasn’t written to me ________ .\nA) for last month\nB) during last month\nC) since last month\nD) a month ago\n85. It was ________ that we felt tired when we arrived.\nA) a so long travel\nB) such a long travel\nC) such a long journey\nD) a so long journey\n86. Is this ________ looking for?\nA) you were\nC) what were you\n\n90. They ________ on holiday in Switzerland and became good friends.\nA) found\nB) knew\nC) met\nD) encountered\n\n66. I’ve brought you ________ flowers for your birthday.\nA) few\nB) a few\nC) little\nD) a little\n\n91. They were very happy when they ________ the end of their journey.\nA) arrived\nB) arrived to\nC) arrived at\nD) reached at\n\n67. He didn’t know ________ or stay at home.\nA) to go\nB) if that he should go\nC) if to go\nD) whether to go\nD) opening\n\n69. Are you interested ________ tennis tomorrow?\nA) in playing\nB) for playing C) on playing\n\nD) to play\n\n70. I wouldn’t rely ________ him if I were you.\nA) to\nB) for\nC) on\n\nD) in\n\n71. Her father didn’t let her ________ out with him.\nA) to go\nB) go\nC) going\n\n92. He ________ .\nA) robbed me my coat\nC) robbed my coat from me\n\nC) How\n\n94. If you don’t ________ smoking you’ll never get better.\nA) give off\nB) give out\nC) give from\nD) give up\nIn this series of questions, three words have the same sound but\none does not. Choose the one that does not.\n\nD) that she went\n\n95. A) love\n\nB) move\n\nC) above\n\nD) glove\n\n96. A) gone\n\nB) bone\n\nC) stone\n\nD) own\n\n97. A) want\n\nB) plant\n\nC) aunt\n\nD) can’t\n\n98. A) weak\n\nB) peak\n\nC) break\n\nD) speak\n\n99. A) low\n\nB) cow\n\nC) grow\n\nD) slow\n\n100. A) eyes\n\nB) rise\n\nC) price\n\nD) dies\n\nD) So\n\n74. I’m going to the passport office ________ .\nA) to stamp my passport\nB) for stamping my passport\nC) to have stamped my passport\nD) to have my passport stamped\n\nBook 1 Part E\n\nB) stole me my coat\nD) stole my coat from me\n\n93. ________ at the door before you come into the room.\nA) Hit\nB) Knock\nC) Touch\nD) Strike\n\n72. Don’t wait for me if you ________ .\nA) have a hurry\nB) are in a hurry\nC) have speed\nD) are in a speed\n73. ________ beautiful flowers!\nA) What a\nB) What\n\nB) that you were\nD) what you were\n\n89. I don’t think I could ________ another night without sleep.\nA) stand\nB) support\nC) put up\nD) carry\n\n65. They’ll hurt ________ if we don’t stop them fighting.\nA) one to another\nB) one the other\nC) each the other\nD) each other\n\n68. Would you mind ________ the window?\nA) that I open B) open\nC) to open\n\nD) to\n\n82. “I went to the cinema last night.” “So ________ ”\nA) I have\nB) have I\nC) I did\nD) did I\n\n210\n\nIntermediate test 4\n\nINTERMEDIATE TEST - 5\n23. It was raining, ________ was a pity.\nA) what\nB) that\nC) the which\n\nChoose the correct Answer. Only one answer is correct.\nMy wife and I went to the Airport to meet some friends. Their plane\nlanded but they weren’t on it.\n“__1__ if there is a massage for us,” my wife said.\n“They __2__ the plane. Or perhaps they __3__ from coming for\nsome reason.”\nAfter __4__ information At the information desk without success, I\nhad an idea” __5__ their letter?” I asked my wife. She found it in her\nhandbag.\n“Here you Are,” she said. “We __6__ at 10 o’clock on the 7th and\n__7__ us.”\n“But today’ s the 6th,” I said. “We should have looked at the date\nbefore. If we had, we wouldn’t have had this journey for nothing.”\n“How silly!” my wife said. “ I __8__ this letter around for days\nwithout looking at it.”\n\nD) which\n\nB) as\nD) alike\n\n25. I’m going away for a ________ .\nA) holiday of a week\nB) week holiday\nC) holiday week\nD) week’s holiday\n26. Why ________ ? It’s not very important.\nA) to worry\nB) worry\nC) you are worried\nD) you worry\n27. I don’t like ________ at me.\nA) them shouting\nC) their shout\n\n28. It often snows ________ January.\nA) on\nB) in\nC) for\n\nD) at\n\n29. I’ll meet you again ________ the weekend.\nA) by\nB) on\nC) at\n\nD) for\n\nA) Let’s see\n\n2.\n\nA) can have missed\nC) can have lost\n\nB) may have missed\nD) may have lost\n\nA) would be prevented\nC) have been prevented\n\nB) would be avoided\nD) have been avoided\n\n4.\n\nA) asking for\n\nC) asking\n\n5.\n\nA) Do you yet have\nC) Have you yet got\n\nB) Do you already have\nD) Have you still got\n\n31. He wasn’t ________ to lift the case.\nA) too strong\nB) enough strong\nC) strong enough\nD) so strong\n\n6.\n\nA) Are arriving\nC) will be arrive\n\nB) would arrive\nD) will be arrived\n\n32. He can climb trees ________ a monkey.\nA) as\nB) like\nC) the same that D) similarly than\n\n7.\n\nA) want you to wait\nC) would like you to meet\n\nB) want that you look for\nD) would like that find\n\n33. He ________ lives in the house where he was born.\nA) already\nB) yet\nC) still\nD) every\n\n8.\n\nA) am carrying\nC) carry\n\nB) have been carrying\nD) must carry\n\n34. It’s ten o’clock in the morning so he’s still ________.\nA) at the bed B) at bed\nC) in bed\nD) in the bed\n\n9.\n\nI’ve often ________ at hotel.\nA) remained\nB) rested\n\nC) stayed\n\n35. He was a good swimmer so he ________ swim to the river bank\nwhen the boat sank.\nA) could\nB) might\nC) succeeded to D) was able to\n\nB) to ask for\n\nD) We are seeing\n\nB) them shout\nD) that they shout\n\n1.\n\n3.\n\nB) Let’s to see C) Will we see\n\n24. Your car is ________ mine.\nA) the same that\nC) similar to\n\