    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n39. Have you got match? I’ve left my ________ at home.\nA) cigarette lighter\nB) cigarettes lighter\nC) cigarette’s lighter\nC) lighter for cigarettes\n\nD) race\n\n14. The weather ________ says it will rain tomorrow.\nA) provision\nB) forecast\nC) advertisementD) advise\n\n40. That’s the dog ________ .\nA) we’ve been looking after\nB) after which we’ve been looking\nC) what we’ve been looking after\nD) we’ve been taking care for\n\n15. There are a lot of mistakes in this exercise. I’ll have to ________ it\nagain with you.\nA) come though B) go over\nC) repass\nC) instruct\n16. If there are no buses, we’ll have to take a taxi. We must get there\n________ .\nA) somehow or other\nB) somewhere or other\nC) on one way or another\nD) anyway or other\n17. ________ I read, the more I understand.\nA) The more\nB) So much\nC) How much\n\nD) doesn’t she\n\n41. I made him ________ what I had told him.\nA) repeating\nB) that he repeated\nC) repeat\nD) to repeat\n42. I was ________ tired that I had to rest.\nA) so much\nB) so\nC) enough\n\nD) For how much\n\nD) too\n\n18. ________ he does his work, I don’t mind what time he arrives at the\noffice.\nA) So far as\nB) So long as C) In case\nD) Meanwhile\n\n43. He ________ live in the country than in the city.\nA) prefers\nB) likes better to\nC) had better\nD) would rather\n\n19. ________ entering the hall, he found everyone waiting for him.\nA) At\nB) While\nC) On\nD) In\n\n44. He ________ his sister.\nA) remembers me of\nC) reminds me of\n\n20. It’s years ________ a picture.\nA) that I don’t paint\nC) since I painted\n\n45. Put on your raincoat ________ it rains.\nA) because\nB) for\nC) in any case\n\nB) that I didn’t paint\nD) ago I painted\n\n21. I found the first question ________ .\nA) to be easy B) the easy\nC) that it was easy\n\nD) in case\n\nIn this series of questions, three words have the same sound but\none does not. Choose one that