    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nThey are moving from their old apartment to a new house. They are\ntaking all their furniture with a ______.\nA) car\nB) lorry\nC) tanker\nD) train\n\n14. When it is ______, it is not bright or shiny.\nA) sunny\nB) windy\nC) dull\n\nD) clear\n\n15. In ______, it snows a lot.\nA) summer\nB) winter\n\nD) spring\n\n8.\n\nA ______ is similar to bicycle, but it has engine which help itself to\nmove more quickly than bicycle.\nA) horse\nB) motor-cycle C) car\nD) bus\n\n9.\n\nThe ______ will arrive at Amsterdam railway station at 3:00 PM.\nA) train\nB) plane\nC) bus\nD) truck\n\nC) autumn\n\n10. Fifty students and four teachers were traveling in a ______.\nA) bus\nB) van\nC) truck\nD) taxi\n\nBook 2 Part A\n\n232\n\nClassified topics\n\nSYNONYMS\n\nTEST MASTER\n\nFind the synonym of the following words written in capitals.\n1.\n\nHe LOOKS at himself in the glass.\nA) puts\nB) likes\nD) stares\nE) stands\n\nC) sees\n\n2.\n\nShips and AIRCRAFTS are often equipped with radio telephones.\nA) planes\nB) trains\nC) railroads\nD) highways\nE) boats\n\n3.\n\nHemingway is a FAMOUS writer.\nA) well-known\nB) unknown\nD) interesting\nE) loved\n\n4.\n\n20. We took the book last week and now we must GIVE it back.\nA) take\nB) return\nC) revise\nD) copy\nE) hold\n21. Switzerland helps developing countries to TRAIN their skilled\npersonnel.\nA) inform\nB) prepare\nC) learn\nD) give\nE) study\n\nC) good\n22. The girl was so ATTRACTIVE that I constantly looked at her.\nA) simple\nB) plain\nC) ugly\nD) pretty\nE) quick\n\nThe children know that the sun RISES in the east.\nA) wakes up\nB) reaches\nC) appears\nD) sets\nE) watches\n\n5.\n\nThe teacher ASKED why he had missed so many classes.\nA) replied\nB) informed\nC) wondered\nD) answered\nE) said\n\n6.\n\nI don’t want to know what they are TALKING about.\nA) taking\nB) speaking\nC) coming\nD) leaving\nE) saying\n\n7.\n\nThe game they LIKED best was writing short stories of their own.\nA) found\nB) did\nC) enjoyed\nD) wanted\nE) wished\n\n8.\n\nMy friend was sorry as his father was DEAD.\nA) killed\nB) living\nD) was ill\nE) was alive\n\n9.\n\n19. They BEGAN to work together twenty years ago.\nA) finished\nB) stayed\nC) continued\nD) started\nE) gave up\n\n23. My parents WENT TO Moscow in May and they will come back in\nJune.\nA) started\nB) set out\nC) visited\nD) left for\nE) left\n24. If your friend is seriously ill you should GO TO SEE him.\nA) ask about\nB) leave\nC) see\nD) visit\nE) approach\n\nC) came\n\nMy friends can use my notes when they are ILL.\nA) sick\nB) hard\nC) fresh\nD) fine\nE) fear\n\n11. She said that she WAS GOING to live in London.\nA) intended\nB) came\nC) planned\nD) went\nE) left\n\nC) bright\n\n13. They had a big house and AT THE BACK OF it there was a small lake.\nA) behind\nB) in front of\nC) between\nD) over\nE) near\n\nC) badly\n\n27. “Will you GO ON, Ashley?” said the teacher.\nA) start\nB) finish\nD) continue\nE) begin\n\nC) stop\n\nB) came\nD) made\n\n29. I ENJOYED the trip very much.\nA) was happy\nB) interested in\nD) was surprised\nE) was glad\n\nC) liked\n\n30. She is a doctor and ALSO a student.\nA) else\nB) too\nD) neither\nE) so\n\nC) either\n\n31. His HOLIDAY by the sea was like a dream.\nA) rest\nB) rested\nD) stay\nE) life\n\nC) walk\n\n33. The child couldn’t find his ball because he had PUT it under the bed.\nA) take\nB) took\nC) carried\nD) place\nE) placed\n\nC) after that\n\n16. We shall be REACHING the station in 15 minutes.\nA) moving to\nB) leaving for\nC) staying at\nD) getting to\nE) taking from\n17. She saw at once that something terrible had HAPPENED.\nA) solved\nB) decided\nC) understood\nD) heard\nE) taken place\n\n34. The streets of Tashkent are WIDE and straight.\nA) broad\nB) beautiful\nD) long\nE) plain\n\nC) narrow\n\n35. The school he goes to is NEAR his house.\nA) closed\nB) far\nD) about\nE) by\n\nC) not far from\n\n36. There was an old man in a barge, whose nose was exceedingly LARGE.\nA) tiny\nB) huge\nC) minute\nD) wide\nE) small\n\n18. She became angry and BEGAN to shout at them.\nA) finished\nB) stopped\nC) started\nD) set\nE) was over\n\nBook 2 Part A\n\n26. That wasn’t pronounced CORRECTLY.\nA) wrongly\nB) exactly\nD) good\nE) well\n\n32. The housewife TASTED the soup and said it was delicious.\nA) cooked\nB) tried\nC) tried on\nD) took\nE) gave\n\n14. TWO HUNDRED YEARS ago the square yard was very clean.\nA) many years\nB) two week\nC) two centuries\nD) a fortnight\nE) two months\n15. I am not going to write any more NOW.\nA) then\nB) at the moment\nD) early\nE) before\n\nC) once\n\n28. What HAPPENED to you?\nA) was result of\nC) was the matter with\nE) was glad\n\n10. Our classes usually ARE OVER at 7 in the evening.\nA) go on\nB) continue\nC) finish\nD) begin\nE) succeed\n\n12. He thought that he was very SILLY.\nA) clever\nB) foolish\nD) wise\nE) strong\n\n25. I would like to speak to you IMMEDIATELY.\nA) right now\nB) just once\nD) later\nE) in 2 days\n\n233\n\nSynonyms\n\n37. At the age of 17 he LEFT school and went to work at the factory.\nA) graduated\nB) went out\nC) entered\nD) stopped\nE) quitted\n\n55. He WENT ON sleeping while we took him into our house.\nA) continued\nB) spoke\nC) stopped\nD) went\nE) finished\n\n38. I’ll LEND you my book if you return it to me.\nA) take\nB) show\nD) send\nE) get\n\nC) give\n\n56. How are you? I am FINE thanks.\nA) so-so\nB) not well\nD) sick\nE) in low spirits\n\nC) O.K.\n\n39. The festival STARTED in Berlin.\nA) began\nB) go on\nD) was held\nE) opened\n\nC) went on\n\n57. There is a SMALL boat with a man in it.\nA) stout\nB) large\nD) tidy\nE) thin\n\nC) little\n\n40. I like to CLEAN my room.\nA) wash\nB) white - wash\nD) tidy up\nE) sweep\n\nC) paint\n\n41. This film IS ON at the “Friendship” cinema.\nA) is shown\nB) performs\nD) goes\nE) does\n\nFind the synonym of the following words:\n\nC) runs\n\n42. Mr. Brown was very happy as he HAD RETURNED from his\nhometown.\nA) had come back\nB) had seen\nC) had received\nD) had asked\nE) had gone\n43. He ENTERED the shop and wanted to buy a shirt, but it was too\nexpensive.\nA) wanted\nB) arrived\nC) came into\nD) got\nE) reached\n44. I WISH I hadn’t gone to the pictures.\nA) take\nB) stay\nD) argue\nE) spend\n\nC) reply\n\n46. Mark Twain VISITED the Crimea in 1867.\nA) went to\nB) returned\nD) started\nE) left\n\nC) ran\n\nC) expression\n\nD) search\n\n59. Explain\nA) Mix\n\nB) define\n\nC) protest\n\nD) train\n\n60. Fine\nA) poor\n\nB) excellent\n\nC) inferior\n\nD) bad\n\n61. Private\nA) general\n\nB) personal\n\nC) community\n\nD) public\n\n62. Large\nA) thin\n\nB) great\n\nC) long\n\nD) soft\n\n63. Crazy\nA) cruel\n\nB) chubby\n\nC) wild\n\nD) mad\n\n64. Fundamental\nA) awful\n\nB) absurd\n\nC) vain\n\nD) basic\n\n65. Famous\nA) well off\n\nB) needy\n\nC) rich\n\nD) well-known\n\n66. Take off\nA) put on\n\nB) dress\n\nC) wear\n\nD) remove\n\n67. Annual\nA) yearly\n\nB) daily\n\nC) monthly\n\nD) weekly\n\n68. Region\nA) farm\n\nB) area\n\nC) beach\n\nD) source\n\n69. Way\nA) bridge\n\nB) road\n\nC) railway",
    "material_type": "notes",
    "is_premium": false
  },
