    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nD) field\n\n70. Estimate\nA) guess\n\nB) inform\n\nC) miss\n\nD) confuse\n\n71. Error\nA) mistake\n\nB) correct\n\nC) result\n\nD) right\n\n72. Actually\nA) shortly\n\nB) timely\n\nC) briefly\n\nD) really\n\n73. Define\nA) explain\n\nB) protest\n\nC) train\n\nD) mix\n\n74. Want\nA) hesitate\n\nB) detest\n\nC) refuse\n\nD) wish\n\n75. Fresh\nA) moldy\n\nB) new\n\nC) rotten\n\nD) stale\n\n76. Start\nA) finish\n\nB) come\n\nC) begin\n\nD) leave\n\n77. Mature\nA) infant\n\nB) child\n\nC) young\n\nD) adult\n\n78. Remember\nA) offer\n\nB) forget\n\nC) advice\n\nD) recollect\n\nC) the same time\n\n48. Soon I FOUND OUT that she had left for Italy.\nA) saw\nB) learned\nD) knew\nE) recognized\n\nC) heard\n\n49. Argentina is LARGER than Great Britain.\nA) wider\nB) older\nD) bigger\nE) richer\n\nC) better\n\n50. Pete promised to take our PICTURE but didn’t keep his word.\nA) give\nB) bring\nC) photograph\nD) paint\nE) draw\n51. Every spring the school leavers HAVE their diplomas.\nA) fail\nB) carry\nC) bring\nD) organize\nE) take\n52. If you can type 100 words a minute and you would like more\nresponsibility, please CALL 01-722.\nA) shout\nB) explain\nC) cry\nD) utter\nE) phone\n53. Samuel told me that they were PLANNING to see the gallery in a\nfew days.\nA) staying\nB) playing\nC) going\nD) starting\nE) coming\n54. I liked to read books about TRAVELS in my holiday.\nA) rests\nB) walks\nC) plays\nD) journeys\nE) balls\n\nBook 2 Part A\n\nB) question\n\nC) desire\n\n45. Why don’t they ANSWER my question?\nA) say\nB) ask\nD) reform\nE) report\n\n47. I have been to Tashkent A NUMBER OF TIMES.\nA) several times\nB) some time\nD) any time\nE) in no time\n\n58. Investigation\nA) option\n\n234\n\nSynonyms\n\n79. Empty\nA) filled\n\nB) vacant\n\n80. Gift\nA) present\n\nB) punishment C) penalty\n\nD) fine\n\n81. Area\nA) source\n\nB) farm\n\nC) beach\n\nD) region\n\n82. Fortune\nA) luck\n\nB) belief\n\nC) religion\n\nD) faith\n\n83. Personal\nA) public\n\nB) community\n\nC) general\n\nD) private\n\n84. Watch\nA) look at\n\nB) seek\n\nC) think\n\nD) read\n\n85. Far\nA) nearby\n\nB) near\n\nC) distant\n\nD) close\n\n86. Quantity\nA) month\n\nB) sound\n\nC) discount\n\nD) amount\n\n87. Below\nA) near\n\nB) under\n\nC) above\n\nD) next to\n\n88. Kind\nA) rude\n\nB) gentle\n\nC) intelligent\n\nD) brainy\n\n89. Narrow\nA) soft\n\nB) long\n\nC) thin\n\nD) brief\n\n90. Pardon\nA) forgive\n\nB) forbid\n\nC) allow\n\nD) promise\n\n91. Shout\nA) whisper\n\nB) whistle\n\nC) blow\n\nD) yell\n\n92. Enter\nA) get in\n\nB) desert\n\nC) abandon\n\nD) quit\n\n93. Pleased\nA) sad\n\nB) happy\n\nC) unhappy\n\nD) angry\n\n94. Beautiful\nA) ugly\n\nB) sorrowful\n\nC) plain\n\nD) pretty\n\n95. Little\nA) large\n\nB) huge\n\nC) small\n\nD) big\n\n96. Active\nA) slow\n\nB) idle\n\nC) poor\n\nD) energetic\n\n97. Border\nA) density\n\nB) altitude\n\nC) edge\n\nD) surface\n\n98. End\nA) compare\n\nB) start\n\nC) finish\n\nD) move\n\n99. Old\nA) elderly\n\nB) raw\n\nC) immature\n\nD) young\n\n100. Ask\nA) response\n\nB) reply\n\nC) question\n\nD) call\n\nBook 2 Part A\n\nC) full\n\nD) deep\n\n235\n\nSynonyms\n\nANTONYMS\n\nTEST MASTER\n\nFind the antonym of the following words written in capitals.\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\n4.\n\n5.\n\n6.\n\n7.\n\n8.\n\n9.\n\nI’ll have to take the PUPILS into the hills.\nA) teachers\nB) schoolchildren\nD) students\nE) boys\nShe is the WORST student in our group.\nA) good\nB) bad\nD) best\nE) nice\nBreakfast is the FIRST meal of the day.\nA) important\nB) main\nD) last\nE) next\nHe is an enemy, REMEMBER.\nA) keep in mind\nB) remind\nD) forget\nE) believe\n\nC) kids\n\n19. The prince ran after her and saw the pretty shoe which the girl HAD\nLOST.\nA) had found\nB) had left\nC) had forgotten\nD) had forgiven\nE) didn’t find\n\nC) badly\n\n20. It was MIDNIGHT and Cinderella ran away from the palace.\nA) early in the morning B) late night\nC) midday\nD) early night\nE) night\n\nC) last but one\n\n21. They OFTEN stay at the college after classes.\nA) always\nB) seldom\nD) ever\nE) early\n\nC) usually\n\nC) recall\n\n22. Long ago the streets of this town were DIRTY.\nA) clean\nB) narrow\nD) broad\nE) long\n\nC) wide\n\n23. He STARTED painting at a very early age and became famous at 27.\nA) began\nB) gave up\nC) get up\nD) continued\nE) went on\n\nHer luggage was so HEAVY that she asked the young man to help\nher.\nA) easy\nB) large\nC) least\nD) light\nE) vast\nHer English is POOR.\nA) excellently\nD) good\n\nB) unsatisfactory\nE) not good\n\nFebruary is the SHORTEST month in the year.\nA) largest\nB) farthest\nD) highest\nE) biggest\n\nC) bad\n\n24. The travelers came to the hotel, LEFT their luggage there and went\nfor a walk in the town.\nA) kept\nB) raised\nC) caught\nD) took\nE) picked out\n\nC) longest\n\n25. He began TO EARN money very early.\nA) to change\nB) to touch\nD) to sweep\nE) to tear\n\n26. It was not EASY for him to find a job in such a long time.\nA) difficult\nB) pleasant\nC) necessary\nD) heavy\nE) dark\n\nTAKING a piece of chalk the pupil on duty began writing on the\nboard.\nA) giving\nB) sending\nC) bringing\nD) spending\nE) belonging\nI liked the END of the story most of all.\nA) beginning\nB) middle\nD) meaning\nE) part\n\nC) to spend\n\n27. The weather was nice and children didn’t want to stay INSIDE.\nA) at home\nB) in the country\nC) out\nD) outside\nE) garden\n\nC) starting\n\n28. Let’s open the window. It’s very HOT here.\nA) dark\nB) cold\nD) foggy\nE) easy\n\nC) stuffy\n\n10. Our farm is in the COUNTRY.\nA) street\nB) valley\nD) town\nE) park\n\nC) forest\n\n11. I WAS RIGHT last night, wasn’t I?\nA) was over\nB) were ill\nD) was wrong\nE) was busy\n\nC) correct\n\n29. You speak so FAST that it is nearly impossible to follow what you\nsay.\nA) weak\nB) low\nC) slow\nD) quick\nE) quite\n\nC) give\n\n30. GO OUT OF the room, please, it’s very stuffy here.\nA) come out\nB) leave\nC) leave for\nD) stay in\nE) useful\n\n12. I don’t REMEMBER where I left my umbrella.\nA) know\nB) forget\nD) notice\nE) support\n13. What is it then, my SON?\nA) girl\nB) boy\nD) dear\nE) friend\n\nC) daughter\n\n31. A DARK cloud having appeared in the sky, we decided to stay at\nhome.\nA) bright\nB) heavy\nC) white\nD) cloudless\nE) merry\n\n14. Some of them BEGAN to talk to me.\nA) started\nB) finished\nD) ended\nE) founded\n\nC) was over\n\n32. He says they will go to the TOP of the hill next\nA) near\nB) above\nD) under\nE) downstairs\n\n15. The hall was FULL with spectators.\nA) easy\nB) empty\nD) ready\nE) late\n\nC) vacant\n\nC) bottom\n\n33. They have the SHORT road and it will take them twenty minutes to\nget to the village.\nA) big\nB) large\nC) not strong\nD) long\nE) rising\n\n16. There are many other BIG cities in Great Britain with more than a\nmillion inhabitants.\nA) large\nB) short\nC) small\nD) great\nE) low\n\n34. That will do. Your answer is quite RIGHT. Your mark is good.\nA) correct\nB) good\nC) bad\nD) wrong\nE) exact\n\n17. I can’t understand why you are so BUSY at home.\nA) engaged\nB) sleepy\nC) afraid\nD) free\nE) angry\n\n35. Suddenly we heard a HIGH thin voice.\nA) tall\nB) small\nD) low\nE) long",
