    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n19. His country cottage ________ the amenities of his London flat.\nA) missed\nB) overlooked\nC) neglected\nD) ignored\nE) lacked\n\n39. My rifle was not ________, so I did not hit anything.\nA) from the best\nB) for the better\nC) of the best\nD) for the best\nE) of the better\n\n20. The victory was ________ annually by a ten-gun salute.\nA) memorized\nB) commemorated\nC) reminded\nD) recapitulated\nE) remembered\n\n40. Any student who ________ his homework is unlikely to pass his\nexamination.\nA) reduces\nB) neglects\nC) practices\nD) denies\nE) offends\n\nBook 2 Part D\n\n309\n\nTest 7\n\nTEST 8\n1.\n\nYesterday the pound fell to a ________ low level against the dollar,\naccording to this morning news.\nA) final\nB) major\nC) record\nD) remote\nE) last\n\n2.\n\nEven the most detached and indifferent spectator can be ________\naway by enthusiasm at a horserace.\nA) carried\nB) moved\nC) excited\nD) stirred\nE) swept\n\n3.\n\n21. The Stephenson’s’ house was ________ by thieves last night.\nA) broken into\nB) broken up\nC) broken off\nD) broken down\nE) broken in\n22. The fishermen said that the high wind had made the sea very _______.\nA) calm\nB) uneven\nC) undulating\nD) rough\nE) hard\n23. Three masked men ________ the city bank early this morning.\nA) robbed\nB) attacked\nC) stole\nD) took\nE) spoilt\n\nThe young performers ________ and held the audience’s attention\nfrom the moment the curtain went up.\nA) caught\nB) gathered\nC) snatched\nD) took\nE) trapped\n\n4.\n\nShe was very ________ when I told her my pet dog had died.\nA) sympathetic\nB) just\nC) helpful\nD) pitiful\nE) friendly\n\n5.\n\nWhat were John and Mary ________ about when you came into the\nroom?\nA) speaking\nB) discussing\nC) saying\nD) telling\nE) talking\n\n6.\n\nI don’t smoke, but I don’t object to ________ people smoking.\nA) different\nB) another\nC) other\nD) alternative\nE) unlike\n\n7.\n\nI like your new red dress, the color ________ you.\nA) fits\nB) looks\nC) suits\nD) likes\nE) seems\n\n8.\n\nMr. Jones wants to know if he can have a ________ with you.\nA) argument\nB) word\nC) lecture\nD) speech\nE) conversation\n\n9.\n\nMrs. Brown has cleaned the house from ________ to bottom.\nA) attic\nB) first floor\nC) top\nD) roof\nE) upstairs\n\n24. I can’t remember ________ told me Mary had gone to Spain.\nA) which\nB) what\nC) that\nD) who\nE) whose\n25. Can you tell the ________ between margarine and butter?\nA) opposite\nB) change\nC) alteration\nD) difference\nE) sameness\n26. Could you give me a ________? I’ve forgotten my matches.\nA) flame\nB) light\nC) fire\nD) illumination\nE) flare\n27. The Company gave my father a gold watch when he ________.\nA) replaced\nB) reformed\nC) retired\nD) retreated\nE) rearranged\n28. You can’t ________ how frightened I was when I first saw an elephant.\nA) suppose\nB) assume\nC) propose\nD) wonder\nE) imagine\n29. When my sister was in hospital, she was ________ by a well-known\nsurgeon.\nA) worked on\nB) carried on\nC) operated on\nD) turned on\nE) passed on\n30. If you ask Martin, he will explain ________ of cricket to you.\nA) the orders\nB) the arrangements\nC) the regulations\nD) the preparations\nE) the rules\n\n10. Alice is tall and slim and has a beautiful ________.\nA) position\nB) shape\nC) form\nD) figure\nE) size\n\n31. We arrived late because there was a traffic ________.\nA) stop\nB) jam\nC) holding\nD) suspension\nE) confusion\n\n11. Mrs. Brown’s children have very good manners because they have\nbeen well ________.\nA) brought out\nB) brought in\nC) brought together\nD) brought up\nE) brought round\n12. My father is very ________ with his hands.\nA) curious\nB) interested\nD) intelligent\nE) clever\n\n32. I had to wait ________ for an answer to my letter.\nA) a long day\nB) a period\nC) an interval\nD) a stage\nE) a long while\n\nC) interesting\n\n13. Mrs. Brown is offering a ________ of £50 to anyone who finds her\ndiamond ring.\nA) prize\nB) price\nC) reward\nD) money\nE) total\n\nC) suits\n\n34. I am very ________ in architecture.\nA) interested\nB) interesting\nD) informed\nE) intelligent\n\nC) concerned\n\n35. The Meeting has been ________ till next Thursday.\nA) put by\nB) put off\nC) put over\nD) put in\nE) put away\n\n14. I should be ________ if you would answer my letter by return.\nA) nice\nB) good\nC) glad\nD) cheerful\nE) kind\n\n36. A circle is a different ________ from a square.\nA) shape\nB) shade\nD) style\nE) number\n\n15. He will pass his examination if he works ________.\nA) quietly\nB) strongly\nC) hard\nD) cleverly\nE) loudly\n\nC) sign\n\n37. Could you ________ me £5? I’ll pay you back tomorrow.\nA) pay\nB) borrow\nC) lend\nD) provide\nE) donate\n\n16. Mary is very ________ because she has failed her examination.\nA) excited\nB) afraid\nC) sensitive\nD) sensible\nE) upset\n17. My father told me never ________ a lie.\nA) to do\nB) to make\nD) to recount\nE) to relate\n\n33. Call for me at any time that ________ you.\nA) fits\nB) likes\nD) docs\nE) meets\n\n38. You can’t smoke here. It’s ________.\nA) prevented\nB) allowed\nD) prohibited\nE) ceased\n\nC) to tell\n\nC) stopped\n\n39. I don’t believe you, you must be ________ my leg.\nA) grasping\nB) holding\nC) handling\nD) pulling\nE) stretching\n\n18. Mrs. Brown’s children are always as good as ________.\nA) butter\nB) gold\nC) milk\nD) silk\nE) silver\n\n40. It’s very cold, the temperature is several ________ below zero.\nA) ounces\nB) inches\nC) numbers\nD) degrees\nE) figures\n\n19. My cousin, who lives in France, is ________ me French.\nA) learning\nB) teaching\nC) helping\nD) assisting\nE) instructing\n20. Peter has not got the right ________ for that job.\nA) knowledge\nB) learning\nC) qualifications\nD) abilities\nE) examinations\n\nBook 2 Part D\n\n310\n\nTest 8\n\nTEST 9\n1.\n\n2.\n\n3.\n\n4.\n\n5.\n\n6.\n\n________ you hurry up, you’ll miss the bus.\nA) Because\nB) If\nD) Except\nE) Unless\n\n22. After walking four miles in the pouring rain, the children were\n________.\nA) moist\nB) damp\nC) drowned\nD) humid\nE) drenched\n\nC) Also\n\nThe man jumped out of the window and committed ________.\nA) murder\nB) death\nC) sin\nD) suicide\nE) homicide\n\n23. The Grand Hotel ________ five pounds for a single room with bath.\nA) pays\nB) prices\nC) charges\nD) expends\nE) spends\n\nI was walking along the street when I accidentally _______ my friend.\nA) bumped into\nB) moved into\nC) came into\nD) fell into\nE) saw into\n\n24. The thief ________ my handbag and ran off down the street.\nA) caught\nB) snatched\nC) picked\nD) disconnected\nE) detached\n\nThe doctor took his temperature and felt his ________.\nA) vein\nB) nerve\nC) blood\nD) pulse\nE) muscle\nIt’s my ________ that it’s going to rain.\nA) option\nB) opinion\nD) decision\nE) thought",
