    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n25. I thought the problem of pollution would ________ at the meeting\nbut no one mentioned it.\nA) come in\nB) come over\nC) come to\nD) come up\nE) come round\n\nC) intention\n\n26. Jane’s new blue dress ________ her coat perfectly.\nA) likes\nB) matches\nC) colors\nD) resembles\nE) fits\n\nThis book is too ________, I don’t understand it.\nA) secret\nB) opaque\nC) dark\nD) obscure\nE) blank\n\n7.\n\nShe was very inquisitive and she didn’t ________ to hide her curiosity.\nA) effect\nB) affect\nC) attempt\nD) discover\nE) find\n\n8.\n\nShe wanted to buy a modern dress, she didn’t want an old-________\none.\nA) styled\nB) formed\nC) looked\nD) fashioned\nE) shaped\n\n9.\n\nWhat ________ is your car?\nA) manufacture\nB) construction\nD) mark\nE) assembly\n\n27. When I came in, John and Mary ________ about the best way to\nlearn English.\nA) were saying\nB) were teaching\nC) were speaking\nD) were telling\nE) were talking\n28. Let’s go into the garden and ________ some roses to take to your\nmother.\nA) dig\nB) pick\nC) pull\nD) break\nE) detach\n29. Would you go upstairs and ________ my handbag, please.\nA) take\nB) bring\nC) carry\nD) fetch\nE) obtain\n\nC) make\n\n30. The houses with even numbers are on the left side of the street and\nthose with ________ numbers are on the right.\nA) odd\nB) unequal\nC) irregular\nD) level\nE) divided\n\n10. He was a very ________ driver and had a lot of accidents.\nA) careful\nB) careless\nC) correct\nD) cautious\nE) conscientious\n11. The ________ gave the new film a very good review.\nA) critics\nB) reporters\nC) announcers\nD) interviewers\nE) translators\n\n31. Every morning I do the crossword ________ in the newspaper.\nA) problem\nB) puzzle\nC) question\nD) test\nE) theme\n\n12. Grandmother lets the children do anything they like, so they are\ncompletely ________.\nA) spoilt\nB) damaged\nC) hurt\nD) injured\nE) destroyed\n\n32. There is an index ________ of this book.\nA) in the end\nB) on the end\nD) at the end\nE) with the end\n\nC) from the end\n\n33. It was so cold that the water in the lake ________.\nA) chilled\nB) iced\nC) froze\nD) hardened\nE) boiled\n\n13. The Manager asked me to ________ the contract for my new job.\nA) write\nB) describe\nC) sign\nD) disagree\nE) design\n\n34. John ________ his examination but his brother failed.\nA) succeeded\nB) made\nC) resulted\nD) passed\nE) qualified\n\n14. ______ for the post of Senior Clerk must be received by March 10th.\nA) Proposals\nB) Descriptions\nC) Possibilities\nD) Applications\nE) Offerings\n\n35. The Government will have ________ this proposal very carefully.\nA) to go for\nB) to go after\nC) to go into\nD) to go round\nE) to go under\n\n15. Mr. Hobson has had to ________ his job because of ill-health.\nA) give in\nB) give up\nC) give away\nD) give out\nE) give over\n16. My English teacher ________ me to try for a place at University.\nA) insisted\nB) persisted\nC) proposed\nD) convinced\nE) encouraged\n17. I ________ you £5 that Peter will win the race on Saturday.\nA) gamble\nB) bet\nC) offer\nD) give\nE) risk\n\n36. The Post Office is only a few yards ________.\nA) in the road\nB) on the road\nD) under the road\nE) up the road\n\nC) above the road\n\n37. Will you help me ________ this parcel, please?\nA) tie up\nB) lie down\nD) tie for\nE) tie with\n\nC) tie in\n\n18. Mary had to be taken to hospital after her ________.\nA) dilemma\nB) distraction\nC) happening\nD) accident\nE) occurrence\n\n38. If you didn’t keep scratching that spot on your face, it would soon\n________.\nA) remedy\nB) cure\nC) restore\nD) heal\nE) mend\n\n19. I shall never ________ the time when I was lost in London without\nany money.\nA) remember\nB) recall\nC) forget\nD) recollect\nE) imagine\n\n39. Mary has given me a ________ for chocolate cake.\nA) prescription\nB) description\nC) diet\nD) list\nE) recipe\n40. Mrs. Simpson ________ £1000 to the Dogs’ Home when she died.\nA) remained\nB) left\nC) presented\nD) offered\nE) permitted\n\n20. Mary is almost well again now, but she still looks rather ________.\nA) faded\nB) light\nC) poor\nD) transparent\nE) pale\n21. I feel so sleepy, I can hardly ________ my eyes open.\nA) make\nB) keep\nC) pull\nD) take\nE) bring\n\nBook 2 Part D\n\n311\n\nTest 9\n\nTEST 10\n1.\n\nMy brother ________ his dog not to chase sheep.\nA) has learned\nB) has trained\nC) has educated\nD) has instructed\nE) has informed\n\n21. There were twenty-five ________ waiting in the doctor’s surgery.\nA) customers\nB) visitors\nC) patients\nD) waiters\nE) clients\n\n2.\n\nIs there any ________ of your coming to London again in the Spring?\nA) opportunity\nB) occasion\nC) facility\nD) chance\nE) ability\n\n22. Mr. Brown has a very ________ job as Sales Manager.\nA) responsible\nB) controlled\nC) ordered\nD) dutiful\nE) careful\n\n3.\n\nHe visited an ________ castle in an old part of the city.\nA) antique\nB) ancient\nC) aged\nD) elderly\nE) olden\n\n23. There is a ________ of sugar in Europe at the moment.\nA) want\nB) need\nC) requirement\nD) omission\nE) shortage\n\n4.\n\nPeter is going _______ for the Job as Manager of the Sales\nDepartment.\nA) to propose\nB) to present\nC) to pretend\nD) to submit\nE) to apply\n\n24. Beethoven is my ________ composer.\nA) best\nB) nicest\nD) favorite\nE) first\n\nC) selected\n\n25. I am going to watch the tennis ________ on television this afternoon.\nA) contest\nB) game\nC) match\nD) sport\nE) trial\n\n5.\n\nI don’t think I know him, although his face seems ________.\nA) friendly\nB) known\nC) knowing\nD) familiar\nE) usual\n\n6.\n\nSome people had to escape in boats when the river ______ its banks.\nA) overthrew\nB) overflowed\nC) overcame\nD) overpowered\nE) overhung\n\n26. The doctor told him to keep the tablets in his mouth and ________\nthem slowly.\nA) swallow\nB) suck\nC) bite\nD) drink\nE) eat\n\n7.\n\nIs there a telephone ________ anywhere near here, please?\nA) place\nB) shop\nC) box\nD) compartment\nE) room\n\n27. I can’t open the drawer in my desk, it’s ________.\nA) fixed\nB) bolted\nC) set\nD) stuck\nE) unmoved\n\n8.\n\nFor her wedding the ________ was dressed in white.\nA) bridesmaid\nB) bride\nC) bridegroom\nD) best man\nE) wife\n\n28. Old Mr. Pottinger ________ his pension every Friday.\nA) pays\nB) earns\nC) draws\nD) acquires\nE) obtains\n\n9.\n\nMr. Black ________ to arrive on the 2:30 train.\nA) is anticipated\nB) is hoped\nD) is expected\nE) is proposed\n\n29. Mr. Higgins is quite sure he saw a flying ________ when he was\nwalking home from the pub.\nA) plate\nB) saucer\nC) dish\nD) cup\nE) tray\n\nC) is wanted\n\n10. I always ________ asleep as soon as I get into bed.\nA) fall\nB) go\nC) get\nD) turn\nE) make\n\n30. Please tell Anne that my private affairs are nothing to ________ her.\nA) do with\nB) do for\nC) do over\nD) do down\nE) do in",
