    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n19. I want to know the answers to these questions, so I shall have to\nlook at the ________ at the back of the book.\nA) index\nB) key\nC) register\nD) record\nE) table\n\nBook 2 Part D\n\nC) depressed\n\n40. Lucy says she bought her new trouser suit in ________.\nA) a disposal\nB) a sale\nC) a reduction\nD) an offering\nE) a production\n\n314\n\nTest 12\n\nTEST 13\n1.\n\nWhen he was questioned by the police, the thief didn’t ________\nthe truth.\nA) say\nB) reply\nC) answer\nD) tell\nE) respond\n\n2.\n\nWhen their mother died, the children were _____ by their Aunt\nMary.\nA) brought in\nB) brought round\nC) brought to\nD) brought forward\nE) brought up\n\n3.\n\n4.\n\n5.\n\n21. There is a ________ on the suitcase, but it has no name on it.\nA) paper\nB) ticket\nC) sign\nD) stamp\nE) label\n22. The air hostess told the passengers to ________ their seat belts.\nA) tie\nB) attach\nC) fasten\nD) fix\nE) set\n23. My sister works at a home for the deaf and ________.\nA) mute\nB) dumb\nC) silent\nD) speechless\nE) voiceless\n\nDon’t touch that wire or you may get an electric ________.\nA) shock\nB) current\nC) attack\nD) feeling\nE) surprise\n\n24. The price of this TV set is not listed in the ________.\nA) catalogue\nB) guidebook\nC) directory\nD) record\nE) schedule\n\nMr. Brown thinks he knows ________ about football, but he doesn’t.\nA) anything\nB) everybody\nC) everything\nD) somebody\nE) nobody\n\n25. The police were able to trace the criminal because he left his ________\non the door handle.\nA) fingerprints\nB) finger-nails\nC) fingertips\nD) ringer ends\nE) finger-marks\n\nThe High Street is so narrow that the Council have decided to\n________ it.\nA) increase\nB) extend\nC) widen\nD) lengthen\nE) shorten\n\n6.\n\nYour brother is very tall. What is his exact ________?\nA) size\nB) length\nC) breadth\nD) measure\nE) height\n\n7.\n\nIf Maria comes to England, it will be a good ________ for her to\nimprove her English.\nA) possibility\nB) opportunity\nC) advantage\nD) probability\nE) experience\n\n8.\n\nPlease ________ your hand if you want to ask the teacher a question.\nA) rise\nB) pull\nC) push\nD) lift\nE) raise\n\n9.\n\n________ 100 if you want to speak to the telephone operator.\nA) Ask\nB) Hear\nC) Dial\nD) Describe\nE) Turn\n\n26. Ann refused to take _______ in the preparations for the school\nconcert.\nA) place\nB) part\nC) notice\nD) leave\nE) offence\n27. Any candidate caught ______ in the examination will be disqualified.\nA) deceiving\nB) deluding\nC) conjuring\nD) swindling\nE) cheating\n28. The farmer put a ________ in his field to frighten the birds away from\nhis crops.\nA) scarecrow\nB) monster\nC) demon\nD) goblin\nE) corpse\n29. He has been making money ______ since he started his new business.\nA) head over heels\nB) hand over fist\nC) head to foot\nD) ear to ear\nE) top to toe\n30. It was so cold my fingers were quite ________.\nA) senseless\nB) numb\nD) unconscious\nE) paralyzed\n\n10. Our school ________ for the summer holidays on 10th July.\nA) breaks up\nB) breaks down\nC) breaks in\nD) breaks off\nE) breaks through\n\n31. You should take more exercise if you want to keep ________.\nA) fit\nB) fat\nC) fine\nD) fresh\nE) flat\n\n11. If you’ve got a ________ of cards, I’ll show you some tricks.\nA) packet\nB) collection\nC) pack\nD) set\nE) parcel\n\n32. The twins are so alike that I can never ________ the difference\nbetween them.\nA) tell\nB) say\nC) decide\nD) make\nE) find\n\n12. This church was ________ by the famous architect Archibald Sparrow.\nA) outlined\nB) designed\nC) produced\nD) composed\nE) made\n13. It’s Grandmother’s birthday tomorrow, so don’t forget to wish her\nmany happy ________.\nA) returns\nB) days\nC) anniversaries\nD) years\nE) congratulations\n\n33. I took the doctor’s prescription to the chemist’s to be ____.\nA) made out\nB) made up\nC) made over\nD) made into\nE) made for\n34. My boss has ________ playing golf three afternoons a week.\nA) taken over\nB) taken to\nC) taken for\nD) taken out\nE) taken in\n\n14. The ________ from the airport was very tiring as we had to drive\nthrough the fog.\nA) travel\nB) voyage\nC) flight\nD) journey\nE) crossing\n\n35. The Prime Minister made an excellent ______ in the House yesterday.\nA) discourse\nB) discussion\nC) lecture\nD) speech\nE) talk\n\n15. If I bought a ticket in the lottery, I might ________ £1000.\nA) bet\nB) buy\nC) sell\nD) win\nE) let\n\n36. I have never been on good ________ with my sister-in-law.\nA) responses\nB) exchanges\nC) terms\nD) feelings\nE) affections\n\n16. John hopes to ________ his examination in September.\nA) make\nB) take\nC) do\nD) offer\nE) present\n\n37. The ________ on this tombstone is dated 1742.\nA) description\nB) inscription\nC) recording\nD) outline\nE) engraving\n\n17. When you come to London, I can ________ for the night.\nA) put you down\nB) put you off\nC) put you up\nD) put you right\nE) put you away\n\n38. Have you had any ________ of John lately?\nA) enquiries\nB) news\nD) particulars\nE) facts\n\n18. Your new flat ________ me very much of the one we had in\nBirmingham.\nA) remembers\nB) recalls\nC) recollects\nD) receives\nE) reminds\n\nC) details\n\n39. Did you notice the ________ on Walter’s face when he heard Hugo\nhad been made Manager?\nA) appearance\nB) description\nC) expression\nD) disposition\nE) exposition\n\n19. The deer is one of the shyest ________ animals in existence.\nA) savage\nB) untamed\nC) wild\nD) strange\nE) free\n\n40. Children usually ________ after an illness much more quickly than\nadults.\nA) pick up\nB) pick over\nC) pick on\nD) pick out\nE) pick off\n\n20. Do open the window; this room seems very ________.\nA) moldy\nB) stuffy\nC) smoked\nD) rancid\nE) breathless\n\nBook 2 Part D\n\nC) insensible\n\n315\n\nTest 13\n\nTEST 14\n1.\n\nI had to sign for this letter because it came in ________ envelope.\nA) a recommended\nB) a registered\nC) an endorsed\nD) a receipted\nE) a sealed\n\n2.\n\nWhen I bought this clock I was given a six months’ ________.\nA) reservation\nB) guarantee\nC) undertaking\nD) safeguard\nE) security\n\n3.\n\n4.\n\n5.\n\n6.\n\n7.\n\n8.\n\n9.\n\n21. At the election you must mark your paper, fold it and drop it into\nthe ________ box.\nA) voting\nB) ballot\nC) nomination\nD) selection\nE) electoral\n22. When you return to your country, don’t forget to ________ with me.\nA) keep in hand\nB) keep time\nC) keep in touch\nD) keep in step\nE) keep together\n\nA ________ for the company said that the question of safety\nregulations was being looked into.\nA) speaker\nB) spokesman\nC) officer\nD) reporter\nE) interpreter\n\n23. The corrupt builder wanted to obtain the contract so he offered a\n________ to the civil servant.\nA) bribe\nB) bait\nC) stimulus\nD) tip\nE) bonus",
