    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\n9.\n\nSally ________ a little money every week for her holiday.\nA) puts in\nB) puts off\nC) puts by\nD) puts over\nE) puts upon\n\n30. The notice on the gate said “________ the dog.”\nA) take care of\nB) be careful of\nC) beware of\nD) take notice of\nE) be afraid of\n\nC) agrees\n\n10. My brother has curly hair but mine is quite ________.\nA) even\nB) regular\nC) uneven\nD) level\nE) straight\n\n31. You ought to be ______ yourself for being so rude to old Mrs. Green.\nA) sorry for\nB) unhappy about\nC) ashamed of\nD) repenting for\nE) unfriendly to\n\n11. John always gets very annoyed if he can’t get his own ________.\nA) wish\nB) desire\nC) will\nD) object\nE) way\n\n32. Just as the violinist began to play, one of the ________ on his violin\nbroke.\nA) cords\nB) tapes\nC) strings\nD) wires\nE) chords\n\n12. It’s no use shouting at grandmother, she’s as deaf as a ________.\nA) post\nB) pin\nC) pole\nD) door\nE) wall\n\n33. The little girl woke up screaming because she had had a ________.\nA) daydream\nB) nightmare\nC) fantasy\nD) vision\nE) reverie\n\n13. If you leave that butter in the sun, it will ________.\nA) thaw\nB) dissolve\nC) set\nD) harden\nE) melt\n\n34. Have you any ________ where you left your car keys?\nA) knowledge\nB) information\nC) notion\nD) idea\nE) thought\n\n14. When I peel onions. I can’t stop my eyes ________.\nA) spilling\nB) watering\nC) leaking\nD) dripping\nE) dropping\n\n35. The magistrate ________ the parents for not exercising proper control\nover the delinquent boy.\nA) blamed\nB) faulted\nC) judged\nD) accused\nE) exposed\n\n15. I’m going home tomorrow so I mustn’t forget to buy some ________.\nA) memories\nB) reminders\nC) recollections\nD) souvenirs\nE) remembrances\n16. I caught the train by the skin of my ________.\nA) mouth\nB) teeth\nD) nose\nE) cheeks\n\n36. I’d like to ________ the holiday arrangements once more before we\nleave tomorrow.\nA) go for\nB) go over\nC) go round\nD) go about\nE) go by\n\nC) lips\n\n17. Peter doesn’t drink alcohol, he only drinks ________ drinks.\nA) squashed\nB) crushed\nC) smooth\nD) dry\nE) soft\n\n37. Mr. Brown always ________ his letters to his secretary as soon as he\nhas opened his post.\nA) answers\nB) writes\nC) copies\nD) dictates\nE) replies\n\n18. Whose ________ was it to go for this long, uninteresting walk?\nA) thought\nB) desire\nC) dream\nD) purpose\nE) idea\n\n38. He made a note of the appointment in his ________.\nA) journal\nB) diary\nC) ledger\nD) register\nE) directory\n\n19. When he was running across the field, he ________ a log.\nA) fell down\nB) fell over\nC) fell off\nD) fell into\nE) fell upon\n\n39. How ________ is your house from the station?\nA) long\nB) distant\nD) far\nE) close\n\n20. John put the suitcases in the ________ of the car.\nA) shoe\nB) toe\nC) boot\nD) slipper\nE) foot\n\n40. I have got to get up early tomorrow so I must remember to ________\nmy alarm clock.\nA) time\nB) set\nC) fix\nD) turn\nE) point\n\n21. The doctor gave me ________ for some medicine.\nA) an order\nB) a letter\nC) an instruction\nD) a recipe\nE) a prescription\n\nBook 2 Part D\n\nC) near\n\n317\n\nTest 15\n\nTEST 16\n1.\n\nThe inspector was a very ________ man and rechecked the evidence\nseveral times.\nA) complete\nB) wholesome\nC) thoughtful\nD) thorough\nE) attentive\n\n20. He doubted if he would pass the examination as it was ________\nwhether he would even finish the paper.\nA) wait and see\nB) hit or miss\nC) touch and go\nD) this or that\nE) open to error\n\n2.\n\nMy friend exercises regularly and is in much better _____ than I am.\nA) figure\nB) size\nC) shape\nD) frame\nE) outline\n\n21. My aunt used to pretend that she could tell fortunes from tea ______.\nA) seeds\nB) buds\nC) leaves\nD) leavings\nE) grounds\n\n3.\n\nMr. Brown kept the ________ round his garden neatly clipped.\nA) hedge\nB) fence\nC) railings\nD) plants\nE) flowers\n\n4.\n\nTomorrow is a special ________ night for the guitarist who has injured\nhis hand and can’t play again.\nA) benefit\nB) welfare\nC) merit\nD) charity\nE) goodwill\n\n22. Mr. Sims has walked with a ________ ever since his car accident six\nyears ago.\nA) limp\nB) jog\nC) trot\nD) hop\nE) jump\n\n5.\n\nMr. Jones was always interfering and poking his nose into everyone’s\n________.\nA) situation\nB) job\nC) work\nD) business\nE) life\n\n6.\n\nI can’t ________ the sound of a knife scraping on a plate.\nA) bear\nB) support\nC) sustain\nD) suffer\nE) forbear\n\n7.\n\nI’m sure they couldn’t have arranged it; they must have met\n________.\nA) at random\nB) by chance\nC) with luck\nD) by fate\nE) by design\n\n8.\n\n9.\n\n23. Oh, dear, my pen has ________; can you lend me yours?\nA) run off\nB) run down\nC) run out\nD) run in\nE) run up\n24. Would it be possible to have these photographs ________?\nA) expanded\nB) enlarged\nC) extended\nD) inflated\nE) stretched\n25. Don’t forget to ________ your luggage clearly in case It gets mislaid\nin transit.\nA) print\nB) name\nC) sign\nD) identify\nE) label\n26. The ________ of living has risen by 10% in the last three months.\nA) price\nB) expense\nC) cost\nD) rate\nE) expenditure\n27. Marie often buys clothes at that ________ stall in the market.\nA) second-class\nB) second-best\nC) second-hand\nD) second string\nE) second chance\n\nIf you want to know how to wash that sweater, look at the ________\ninside the collar.\nA) badge\nB) ticket\nC) notice\nD) sign\nE) tab\n\n28. Don’t eat those berries in case they are ________.\nA) poisonous\nB) venomous\nC) infectious\nD) emetic\nE) contagious\n\nOh dear. I don’t seem to have my bag, I must have ________ it in\nthe Post Office.\nA) missed\nB) overlooked\nC) forgotten\nD) left\nE) misplaced\n\n29. I’ve got such a _____ throat I’m sure I must be going to have a cold.\nA) hurt\nB) sensitive\nC) irritable\nD) sour\nE) sore\n30. You can take a short ________ through the woods to the station.\nA) lane\nB) road\nC) highway\nD) cut\nE) alley\n\n10. He had injured his arm badly and had to keep it in a ________ for\nseveral weeks.\nA) cradle\nB) swing\nC) sling\nD) litter\nE) stretcher\n\n31. I’m afraid it will be a long time before we get to the ________ of this\nunpleasant affair.\nA) base\nB) bottom\nC) foundation\nD) foot\nE) basis\n\n11. Peter’s car ________ in the country so he had to walk lo the nearest\nvillage for help.\nA) broke up\nB) broke down\nC) broke away\nD) broke off\nE) broke open\n\n32. John has just passed his driving test, so now he’s on the ________\nfor a cheap car.\nA) outlook\nB) pursuit\nC) lookout\nD) discovery\nE) track\n\n12. She tied a scarf round her head to ________ her hair from the rain.\nA) cover\nB) hide\nC) keep\nD) shelter\nE) protect\n\n33. At the beginning of the war every man under thirty was ________ to\nserve in the armed forces.\nA) called in\nB) called up\nC) called for\nD) called out\nE) called over",
