    "body": "Source: LET English Grammar Test (9000+ Questions).pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nB) very quick\n\nA) the boss\nC) movement\n\nB) is frightening\n\nA) aim for\nC) invent\n\nB) improve\n\n190. To \"think twice\" is to _____.\nB) attack\n\nA) create something\nC) hesitate\n\n174. To \"run away with\" means to _____.\nA) lend\nC) borrow\n\nB) everything\n\n189. To \"think up\" is to _____ something.\n\n173. To \"rip into\" means to _____.\nA) enjoy\nC) savor\n\nB) correct someone\n\n188. \"The works\" is _____.\n\n172. If something \"rings a bell\", it _____.\nA) makes a lot of noise\nC) sounds familiar\n\nB) shout\n\n187. To \"tell something apart\" is to _____.\n\n171. If it's to the \"right and left\" it's _____.\nA) rare\nC) all around\n\nB) lead\n\nB) tell a lie\n\n191. To go \"through thick or thin\" is to _____.\n\nB) steal\n\nA) lose a lot of weight\nB) get married\nC) have many kinds of experiences\n\n175. If it's \"safe and sound\", it's _____.\nA) not allowed\nC) not harmed\n\n192. To \"throw up\" is to _____.\n\nB) beautiful\n\nA) get rid of something\nC) give up\n\nB) vomit\n\n176. If someone says \"same here\", he is _____.\nA) agreeing\nC) disagreeing\n\n193. To \"tip off\" someone is to _____ her.\n\nB) arguing\n\nA) warn\nC) like\n\nB) attack\n\n177. To \"say the word\" means to _____.\nA) give a sign\nC) give up\n\n194. To do something \"to a T\" is to do it _____.\n\nB) apologize\n\nA) badly\nC) shortly\n\nB) perfectly\n\n178. To \"screw up\" is to _____.\nA) do it perfectly\nC) go higher and higher\n\n195. \"Uh-huh\" means the same as _____.\n\nB) make a mess\n\nA) no\nC) maybe\n\nB) yes\n\n179. If you \"see eye to eye\" with someone, you _____ them.\nA) oppose\nC) agree with\n\n196. If it's \"under your nose\", it's _____.\n\nB) encourage\n\nA) well hidden\nC) within sight\n\nB) your fault\n\n180. To \"set your sight\" on something means to _____ something.\nA) aim for\nC) ask for\n\n197. To have the \"upper hand\" is to have _____.\n\nB) look for\n\nA) the advantage\nC) the next go\n\nB) permission\n\n181. To \"shell out\" for something is to _____.\nA) hide it\nC) try to find it\n\n198. If you get \"used to\" something, you _____ it.\n\nB) spend money on it\n\nA) get rid of\nC) become accustomed to\n\nB) take care of\n\n182. If you are \"sick and tired\", you are _____.\nA) exasperated\nC) angry\n\n199. If it's \"up in the air\", it's _____.\n\nB) jealous\n\nA) important\nC) unwanted\n\nB) undecided\n\n183. \"Shut your trap\" is an impolite way of saying \"please _____.\nA) leave\".\nC) be quiet\".\n\n200. \"Under your breath\" means to _____.\n\nB) go away\".\n\nA) whisper\nC) hesitate\n\nB) tell a secret\n\n184. If you are \"stuck up\", you are _____.\nA) snobbish\nC) problematical\n\nBook 3\n\n201. \"Under the sun\" means _____.\n\nB) in trouble\n\nA) it's impossible\nC) on earth\n\n396\n\nB) it's unusual\n\nIdioms\n\n202. If you are \"up front\", you are _____.\nA) bold\nC) brave\n\n219. \"You bet\" means _____.\n\nB) sincere\n\nA) no\nC) if I can\n\n203. \"Under wraps\" means _____.\nA) in secret\nC) in a small space\n\n220. \"You don't say\" shows _____.\nB) with difficulty\n\nA) disbelief\nC) surprise\n\n204. If you are \"up tight\", you are _____.\nA) rich\nC) an executive\n\nB) worried\n\nA) encourages\nC) corrects\n\nB) later\n\nA) never\nC) eventually\n\nB) defeat\n\nA) condemnation\nC) agreement\n\nA) argue\nC) question\n\nA) delicious\nC) frightening\n\nB) horrible\n\n226. To \"zonk-out\" is to _____.\n\nB) forget\n\nA) daydream\nC) fall asleep quickly\n\n210. \"Walking on air\" means you are _____.\nA) happy\nC) upset\n\nB) agree\n\n225. If something is \"yummy\", it's _____.\n\nB) experiences\n\n209. If you \"walk off with\" something, you _____ it.\nA) steal\nC) borrow\n\nB) acceptance\n\n224. If you are a \"yes man\" you always _____.\nB) get excited\n\n208. If someone talks about \"vibes\", they are talking about _____.\nA) feelings\nC) desires\n\nB) constantly\n\n223. \"You can say that again\" shows _____.\n\n207. To \"veg out\" means to _____.\nA) get angry\nC) relax\n\nB) disciplines\n\n222. \"Year in, year out\" means _____.\n\n206. To \"vote down\" is to _____ something.\nA) accept\nC) propose\n\nB) annoyance\n\n221. \"You tell them\" _____ someone.\n\n205. \"Very well\" can mean the same as _____.\nA) no\nC) giving consent\n\nB) certainly\n\nB) get excited\n\n227. To \"zip your lip\" is to _____.\n\nB) depressed\n\nA) shut up\nB) be loud\nC) talk about things you don't know\n\n211. To \"walk all over\" someone is to _____ them.\nA) mislead\nC) impose on\n\n228. To \"zero in on\" is to _____ something.\n\nB) aggravate\n\nA) aim for\nC) alter\n\nB) adjust\n\n212. \"Watch out\" means _____.\nA) be careful\nC) hurry up\n\nB) relax\n\n213. \"Water down\" means to _____.\nA) make stronger\nC) weaken\n\nB) have a beer\n\n214. The \"way the wind blows\" is _____.\nA) how things were\nB) the way things are\nC) how things are going to be\n215. To \"wear on\" someone is to _____ them.\nA) agree with\nC) ignore\n\nB) annoy\n\n216. To say \"word for word\" means to _____.\nA) condense it\nC) say it exactly the same\n\nB) change what was said\n\n217. To \"wet one's whistle\" is to _____.\nA) be happy\nC) have a drink\n\nB) have a problem\n\n218. If you are \"yellow bellied\", you are _____.\nA) brave\nC) cowardly\n\nBook 3\n\nB) conceited\n\n397\n\nIdioms\n\nSlang\n\nTEST 10\n1.\n\nWow, that is a great car!\nA) awesome\n\n2.\n\n21. Don't be such a coward and go do it.\nB) able\n\nC) action\n\nA) cow\n\nAfter staying awake late at night studying, I felt tired the next day.\nA) an angel\nC) an atmosphere\n\nB) carrot\n\nC) chicken\n\n22. He's so relaxed. He never looks rushed.\n\nB) an all-nighter\n\nA) cold\n\nB) curry\n\nC) cool\n\n23. You should phone the police and tell them.\n3.\n\nThis place is so boring, I want some excitement.\nA) action\n\nB) ape\n\nA) corpses\n\nB) cops\n\nC) cowboys\n\nC) aggravation\n24. Watching T.V. all day is turning you into a lazy, good-for-nothing.\n\n4.\n\nHe is such an ill-mannered person.\nA) ant\n\nB) action\n\nA) carrot\n\nB) chair\n\nC) couch potato\n\nC) animal\n25. I'll have to study really hard to pass this test.\n\n5.\n\nI don't want to stay in this dirty, smelly place.\nA) ark\n\nB) armpit\n\nA) cram\n\nB) corn\n\nC) crack\n\nC) apple\n26. The other team beat us even though their best player wasn't there.\n\n6.\n\nI can't believe he put salt in the sugar basin. He's such a stupid person.\nA) an airhead\n\nB) an ace\n\nA) canned\n\nB) creamed\n\nC) cooked\n\nC) an artist\n27. He's really upset because his fish died last night.\n\n7.\n\nDave is the best player on the team.\nA) action\n\nB) apple\n\nA) cooled\n\nB) cracked\n\nC) croaked\n\nC) ace\n28. This is such a simple job. A kid could do it.\n\n8.\n\nThe director gave the little-known actor his first chance.\nA) broad\n\nB) bone\n\nA) cushy\n\nB) cozy\n\nC) comfy\n\nC) break\n29. The disco is really quiet tonight.\n\n9.\n\nThat motorcycle rider looks really tough in his leather outfit.\nA) boss\n\nB) biker\n\nA) dead\n\nB) deep\n\nC) down\n\nC) babe\n30. The boys abandoned the stolen motorbike in the park.",
