    "body": "Source: 02 ENGLISH REVIEWER B.pdf\nSource type: pdf\n\nENGLISH\nLET REVIEWER UNIVERSITY\n1. In one of his poems, the Filipino author Zulueta da Costa said that the Filipinos are like the\nMolave. What figure of speech was used?\na. simile\nb. personification\nc. metaphor\nd. hyperbole\n2. Helen of Troy is the face who launched a thousand ships. What figure of speech is used in\nthe given sentence?\na. ellipsis\nb. synecdoche\nc. alliteration\nd. irony\n3. The captain of the pep squad are working feverishly to boost the team`s morale.\na. pep-squad\nb. are\nc. to boost\nd. team`s morale .\n4. The teachers as well as the guidance counselor is accompanying the students on a field\ntrip.\na. teachers\nb. guidance counselor\nc. is accompanying\nd. on a field trip\n5. Simba and Nala is my favorite characters in The Lion King.\na. and\nb. is\nc. The Lion King\nd. No error’\n6. The committee are meeting on Friday to discuss the details of the charity ball.\na. are meeting\nb. on Friday\nc. to discuss\nd. charity ball\n7. Mumps, which are a dangerous disease, can be prevented through vaccination.\na. Mumps\nb. are\nc. disease\nd. vaccination\n8. The student leaders ______ surveys to determine the students` need since last week.\na. has conducted\nb. have conducted\nc. has conducting\nd. have been conducting\n9. The President _______ the bill on Children`s Right last Monday.\na. vetoes\nb. vetos\nc. vetoed\nd. vetoid\n10. The Committee on Ethics ____ every Friday.\na. meets\nb. meet\nc. has met\nd. have met\n11. It is estimated that in the present century, there ______ about 954 million illiterate adults.\na. is\nb. are\n\nc. was\nd. were\n12. In 1960, 58% of illiterates ______ women; the corresponding figure today ismore than 60%.\na. is\nb. are\nc. was\nd. were\n13. The warm humid air irritated he.\na. irritated he\nb. irritated him\nc. irritation him\nd. irritating him\n14. Keep on reading and you will learn more.\na. Keep on reading\nb. Keep to read\nc. Keep on read\nd. Keeping on reading\n15. Even though Mariel studied hard, she got the highest mark.\na. Even though Mariel studied hard\nb. But Mariel hard\nc. Because Mariel studied hard\nd. While Mariel studied hard\n16. The Carlos Palanca Memorial Award for Literature were given to different literary pieces\nthat excel in their respective genres.\na. were given to different literary pieces\nb. is given by different literary pieces\nc. are given at different literary pieces\nd. is given to different literary pieces\n17. We hike Mt. Apo half an hour.\na. half an hour\nb. for half an hour\nc. at half an hour\nd. by half an hour\n18. Which among the words below has the /sh/ sound?\na. sober\nb. leisure\nc. shallow\nd. salient\n19. Your father isn’t working anymore, __________?\na. is he\nb. isn’t he\nc. has he\nd. hasn’t he\n20. Which among the sound below is a voiceless sound?\na. /dz/\nb ./g/\nc. /z/\nd. /sh/\n21. William Shakespeare showed composure in front of his critics amidst countless derision.\nThe underlined word means ___________.\na. agitation\nb. fear\nc. aplomb\nd. nervousness\n22. Which is the correct form of the mixed conditional?\na. If + Present Perfect s/c + would + infinitive, if + past s/c + would + have + past participle\nb. If + present simple + present simple, if + past perfect s/c + would + have + past participle\nc. If + past perfect s/c + would + have + past participle, if + Present Perfect s/c + would +\ninfinitive\nd. If + present perfect + present simple, if + past perfect s/c + will + have + past participle\n\n23. Which of the following words can be used instead of will in the first conditional?\na. Should, might or could\nb. Should\nc. Should, Were or Had\nd. May, might, can or could\n24. Which is the correct form of the first conditional?\na. If + a present tense + will + infinitive\nb. If + past perfect + past simple\nc. If +past perfect + will + have + past participle\nd. If + past simple + will + ing\n25. Which is the correct ending for this third conditional sentence? If I hadn't eaten so much,\n_________.\na. I won't have felt sick\nb. I wouldn't had felt sick\nc. I wouldn't have felt sick\nd. I wouldn't have feel sick",
